92186471782} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca92a53d-50d7-5e4b-8ec5-4c9924570bd9" :answer-field/key "$¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "17f91135-f9d8-56cf-88b5-eaf7c61a4e5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86690" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬X∧(X∨¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬X∨(X∧¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$ and $¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$; $¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f311c265-2bb0-5ad1-815d-44417f1e31a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471125} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffdf529-09c7-5cab-a876-7f9b20669834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ffdf529-09c7-5cab-a876-7f9b20669834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471126} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8b400c0-9b95-56f2-8848-67709fb87921" :answer-field/key "$\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95b0b167-a547-50ff-8123-620fe621a81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471127} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c742b0-471f-59d1-924e-69676e078128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95b0b167-a547-50ff-8123-620fe621a81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471127} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3cb4bf-3026-5dbf-bb69-ac0bfdbd1d57" :answer-field/key "$A⊂\\text{int}A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0799b728-a09d-5e7c-a241-f50801a2ea50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471129} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8c5826-4aff-5dff-9a12-8d4de0ce361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f8c5826-4aff-5dff-9a12-8d4de0ce361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471130} :answer-field/id #uuid "26da464c-3c67-5b3b-808a-3b3403f4ed69" :answer-field/key "$A-\\text{int}A=∂A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e963f0b-a2c7-5ae0-844a-f3e405d79aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161649" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\ge {y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88f35519cf1aa01bcc9e4fb91b24c2bc2a1a823867ec2670563b0b45f2643a0a.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/64/649c33f1738a35f3d298038bd2cf05d3b435424a4efbbb1e6143cf0d56b2bfd6.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$ is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A.$\n\n- Statement $A⊂\\text{int}A$ is false. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $A⊈\\text{int}A.$\n\n- Statement $A-\\text{int}A=∂A$ is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-\\text{int}A=∂A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{int}\\,A\\cup ∂A=A$; $A-\\text{int}A=∂A$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5c38a40-b0ad-50a0-b1fd-3ca0ed423d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471221} {:answer/id #uuid "b4471eda-3004-561c-b183-28b096dbfdb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5c38a40-b0ad-50a0-b1fd-3ca0ed423d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471221} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1c9fc7-d87b-54a3-a66e-faa888700146" :answer-field/key "If $4\\in {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is even." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3ed57af-e278-5ede-a755-783ce9ed8c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471223} {:answer/id #uuid "761ff025-d2e6-53d2-985e-4816ac004c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "761ff025-d2e6-53d2-985e-4816ac004c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471224} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc9e2ea8-4854-5a7a-8552-15585b54efc9" :answer-field/key "If $4\\notin {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is not even." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f4f384a-3166-5f09-b657-4055cb82802e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471225} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc1fc9d-3e88-590e-be39-355512cb0a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4f384a-3166-5f09-b657-4055cb82802e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471225} :answer-field/id #uuid "c34ffd8a-bcff-52d9-a081-61d20b6aec70" :answer-field/key "If $8$ is not even, then $4\\notin {2,4,8}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d0274f7-9e96-5c91-af2a-50bf61bf0ba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-183341" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $8$ is even **then** $4\\in {2,4,8}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement “If $4\\in {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is even” is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “If $4\\notin {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is not even” is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “If $8$ is not even, then $4\\notin {2,4,8}.$” is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $4\\notin {2,4,8},$ then $8$ is not even” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular and Irregular Singular Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5772d6f-b4c4-5b0f-a341-7bcce7c53ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471441} {:answer/id #uuid "72f28384-9464-531f-83ec-b7d7d44da974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5772d6f-b4c4-5b0f-a341-7bcce7c53ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471441} :answer-field/id #uuid "3de9898a-65aa-5f5c-a471-68d4884d2a25" :answer-field/key "The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}$ are analytic about $x=-3.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472226} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f34e0f7-5c36-57be-8be0-72cd026a3c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471443} {:answer/id #uuid "545a20a3-dc0a-54e0-a437-92e4bb0d8db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f34e0f7-5c36-57be-8be0-72cd026a3c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471443} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e5ae857-3730-5c76-9614-b81b46af3e2a" :answer-field/key "The functions $(x+3)P(x)$ and $(x+3)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-3.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472227} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "331a7444-e6ed-5b95-9c85-51c56d8adc44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471445} {:answer/id #uuid "0dd04662-64d9-59d1-be58-90ecddce155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dd04662-64d9-59d1-be58-90ecddce155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471446} :answer-field/id #uuid "377eb8bf-59f3-5a09-928e-03ed7443b513" :answer-field/key "The point $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39331851-2b44-5819-96f4-7d54c8cd9bd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342366" :question/problem "$$\n(x+3){y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3){y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}{y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{x+3}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Since the denominators of both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ vanish at $x=-3,$ they are *not* analytic about $x=-3.$ So, statement “The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}$ are analytic about $x=-3.$” is false.\n\n- The function\n\n$$\n(x+3)P(x)=(x+3)\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}\n$$\n\n is *not* analytic about $x=-3$ since its denominator vanishes at $x=-3.$ Therefore, statement “The functions $(x+3)P(x)$ and $(x+3)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-3.$” is false.\n\n- Since statement “The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{3}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x+3}$ are analytic about $x=-3.$” is false, $x=-3$ is a singular point. Also, since statement “The functions $(x+3)P(x)$ and $(x+3)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-3.$” is false, it follows that $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point. Thus, statement “The point $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation” is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $x=-3$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90f4b8b6-9087-5496-807d-608724aa78fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470631} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5fbf91-d7c1-5e8c-871e-7c26b0ac303e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb5fbf91-d7c1-5e8c-871e-7c26b0ac303e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470632} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b1dfa9f-9494-59d8-bf95-2c68f20b60a5" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6085786-4948-5140-96cc-351034d2e7a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470633} {:answer/id #uuid "4fce3179-81d2-55bd-a37c-d2f3b28beee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fce3179-81d2-55bd-a37c-d2f3b28beee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470634} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffaaf373-8b01-5dda-82d5-b55d324b703d" :answer-field/key "${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fecb31b-eea1-5984-a868-c589f3e59e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470635} {:answer/id #uuid "0b89d20b-e663-5580-8552-4bead320d1f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fecb31b-eea1-5984-a868-c589f3e59e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470635} :answer-field/id #uuid "a51c31a2-df0f-5d9f-bff0-d622cce2a150" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb972e63-3e46-543b-9a40-0120a6183656" :question/math-academy-id "q-100120" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t-4,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2-t,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=1-t.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(1)q(1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t-4,1-t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t-4){|}_{1}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{1}+(2t-4){|}_{2}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2(1)-4)\\cdot (1-1)+(2(2)-4)\\cdot (1-2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2-t,1-t⟩ \\\\  & =(2-t){|}_{1}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{1}+(2-t){|}_{2}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2-1)\\cdot (1-1)+(2-2)\\cdot (1-2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Let's check if ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t).$ Computing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t-4,2-t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t-4){|}_{1}\\cdot (2-t){|}_{1}+(2t-4){|}_{2}\\cdot (2-t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2(1)-4)\\cdot (2-1)+(2(2)-4)\\cdot (2-2) \\\\  & =-2\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product. So, the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38977e25-5701-59b4-acd7-c07e28c73e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470637} {:answer/id #uuid "795d2da5-60e6-5507-9355-3921ddc95792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "795d2da5-60e6-5507-9355-3921ddc95792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470638} :answer-field/id #uuid "c745d006-d5de-5a2f-9e45-1c00146eae2a" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4846a1f4-412a-515c-8ef9-ed21e5470f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470639} {:answer/id #uuid "e6594a2d-fafd-5fa9-8390-bc86bc6736e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4846a1f4-412a-515c-8ef9-ed21e5470f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470639} :answer-field/id #uuid "4afd9177-d9a1-52e6-9b31-5287eb0e1f1b" :answer-field/key "${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c96296-fbc5-5ab2-9c9f-253e362d1483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470641} {:answer/id #uuid "95e9e5ba-829c-5853-bb9d-a29fdf02c6fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40c96296-fbc5-5ab2-9c9f-253e362d1483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470641} :answer-field/id #uuid "54703d9d-be5e-5e7e-ab6d-caae8559077f" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39aa7418-1a3f-5a9e-9642-6c49cf6dc36a" :question/math-academy-id "q-100129" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t+2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=t+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t+2,t-2⟩ \\\\  & =(2t+2){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t-2){|}_{-1}+(2t+2){|}_{2}\\cdot (t-2){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2(-1)+2)\\cdot ((-1)-2)+(2(2)+2)\\cdot (2-2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{2} \\\\  & =((-1)-2)\\cdot ((-1)+1)+(2-2)\\cdot (2+1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Let's check if ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t).$ Computing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t+2,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(2t+2){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1}+(2t+2){|}_{2}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(2(-1)+2)\\cdot ((-1)+1)+(2(2)+2)\\cdot (2+1) \\\\  & =18\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product. So, the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84280041-92fd-5192-93c9-e48627a8d61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470703} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d9c6cc-655d-587f-a7ea-5270008520aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84280041-92fd-5192-93c9-e48627a8d61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470703} :answer-field/id #uuid "926a2635-c239-5abe-bfe8-8f19a21bad02" :answer-field/key "There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "550f969f-73eb-5d0d-a662-b666c5779497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470705} {:answer/id #uuid "a819f3f3-e7ac-55f9-b274-f932e5858b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "550f969f-73eb-5d0d-a662-b666c5779497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470705} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b1381a-39d6-5006-bdce-409b33804a49" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471858} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afe2e275-0d80-52bd-87be-996bbe232db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470707} {:answer/id #uuid "196f578f-57fc-5e51-97d6-f6020044ee46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe2e275-0d80-52bd-87be-996bbe232db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470707} :answer-field/id #uuid "44ab2c15-20df-54dd-b6fd-3f24203d3699" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7e09caa-cacf-54dd-ae93-0599cdfc3d85" :question/math-academy-id "q-104957" :question/problem "![](images/80/801bb98497bc275acda854447fffee30721bc54b2711ac632c2269f0c1eb64ed.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=-1$” is false. As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $-1\\in Y.$ Hence, $f(x)\\ne -1$ for all $x\\in X.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false. Since statement “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=-1$” is false,  it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false, $f$ is not a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3e0f2a6-da32-5a3e-8038-89e24c09e272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470709} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3452d1-013a-53c5-a2de-57a2d9f941e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab3452d1-013a-53c5-a2de-57a2d9f941e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470710} :answer-field/id #uuid "f96f0323-da65-5381-9e93-1f8171c8674f" :answer-field/key "There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f42b2a-d794-5b15-8036-dcc8c69bb940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470711} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1b2c33-3dfe-58e8-85c4-d8984d0d7ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f42b2a-d794-5b15-8036-dcc8c69bb940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470711} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e50acad-18ff-5772-98c8-8e5ad8ee596a" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4de3c43-fec6-52f9-9554-a815044c92b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470713} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2a6bde-cbe6-5b08-8c2b-1712a8ec63b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4de3c43-fec6-52f9-9554-a815044c92b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470713} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c6bac77-ef1e-593d-badb-80ae667f1767" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **onto**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65240711-5d62-532c-a650-6596f72fcd4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104959" :question/problem "![](images/94/94f14d4a1876588cbfb2abc4a1542d5961587745a6e24aeae270d15f75f834db.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=7$” is true. According to the diagram, we have $f(1)=7$ (we have an arrow from $2\\in X$ to $7\\in Y$). So, there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=7.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false. Consider $y=5.$ As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $5\\in Y.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **onto**” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false, $f$ is not a surjection (also known as *onto*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=7$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ed6a87-c7ef-5ebe-80b8-1327e0527690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470967} {:answer/id #uuid "693db775-71df-5935-b66c-e1e720f6bca0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25ed6a87-c7ef-5ebe-80b8-1327e0527690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470967} :answer-field/id #uuid "72e9d168-8616-5d7a-a0cc-08f65358b7bc" :answer-field/key "$A∨B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76540982-ba2f-5d75-adf4-43d2d26c2645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470969} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a29096-2984-5fc1-8bab-a6bde77b0a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1a29096-2984-5fc1-8bab-a6bde77b0a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470970} :answer-field/id #uuid "5aac595e-10c8-504e-b949-4e22b1e45f80" :answer-field/key "$¬(¬A∧B)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5169fc92-f334-5952-8891-30b740db658e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470971} {:answer/id #uuid "3c0ff306-27ac-502d-b26a-0f286d52abe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c0ff306-27ac-502d-b26a-0f286d52abe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470972} :answer-field/id #uuid "d81243e1-0ab1-5b1d-a3f3-913586a1ef6d" :answer-field/key "$A∨¬B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bbe1542-19d1-529e-93b1-09c0d710a430" :question/math-academy-id "q-127960" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬A∧B)\\,$ | $\\,A∨¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬(¬A∧B)$ and $A∨¬B$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬(¬A∧B)$; $A∨¬B$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ad76e6b-acef-5221-8852-71dc42625bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Correct Function Used to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87cd12d0-6a34-5d69-a052-37dd7b665fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470997} {:answer/id #uuid "2a5c113f-8f85-54df-a191-e6a260a622ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a5c113f-8f85-54df-a191-e6a260a622ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470998} :answer-field/id #uuid "a053ccd6-a515-5e7f-a170-df59bdc9e410" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "499f94a8-9207-510d-9baa-5720b20b1c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470999} {:answer/id #uuid "92e04b93-9fab-5c61-a3ba-0482b966ebc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "499f94a8-9207-510d-9baa-5720b20b1c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470999} :answer-field/id #uuid "82cef237-2c86-5e8e-8666-abbf572a6632" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d53fcefd-cbee-5163-8861-b3c676aacc68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471001} {:answer/id #uuid "7b636524-5e3f-5180-98df-969975052f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d53fcefd-cbee-5163-8861-b3c676aacc68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471001} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a80c0b-1724-53b6-833f-dcb16e1b056b" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d32f310d-7c80-57bd-8ae7-821e89abc170" :question/math-academy-id "q-129901" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2ded513c72c8029b7d2909d2e3b37cbd659c4ba60a7be72c81379626a7a1234.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-1,2]\\times [-1,3],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/77/77c8e1b1aacd29c6d69aa3c641c1641f43ff2aa1467dc713d417641f8b76b066.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal ${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions $\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$ and $\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$. Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(2,3)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function $\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$ equals ${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38d82c66-da81-5da6-99b2-f8009487d231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471233} {:answer/id #uuid "6cfd2ce4-c861-572f-be91-5a67f9259251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38d82c66-da81-5da6-99b2-f8009487d231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471233} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bf3be5b-830f-58c9-a573-942a40eae3d7" :answer-field/key "$3\\,|\\,x$ if and only if $5\\,|x.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3951911-eb29-5274-9d8c-cca561b05b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471235} {:answer/id #uuid "15f517a1-1be6-5193-a806-cc5eb0a13364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3951911-eb29-5274-9d8c-cca561b05b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471235} :answer-field/id #uuid "0990f9ff-8884-566c-89d3-36080e85cb1c" :answer-field/key "If $3\\,|\\,x$ then $3\\,|\\,(x+15),$ or if $3\\,|\\,(x+15)$ then $3\\,|\\,x.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90c29c97-3228-56b1-859a-71e6720b678f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471237} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5acb9a-b1ff-54fa-9112-bdbc02b6fd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e5acb9a-b1ff-54fa-9112-bdbc02b6fd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471238} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfcc4a68-2133-54c2-b0a0-3c81584244b4" :answer-field/key "If $3\\,|\\,x$ then $3\\,|\\,(x+15),$ and if $3\\,|\\,(x+15)$ then $3\\,|\\,x.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9aa776da-0143-5b4b-9d08-2751ea2726a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-183357" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $3\\,|\\,x.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $3\\,|\\,(x+15).$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $3\\,|\\,x$ if and only if $3\\,|\\,(x+15).$\n\n- $3\\,|\\,x$ is equivalent to $3\\,|\\,(x+15).$\n\n- If $3\\,|\\,x$ then $3\\,|\\,(x+15),$ and if $3\\,|\\,(x+15)$ then $3\\,|\\,x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $3\\,|\\,x$ then $3\\,|\\,(x+15),$ and if $3\\,|\\,(x+15)$ then $3\\,|\\,x.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381714 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114dedd9-ed3d-5d25-8616-030ea4bd84c9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Universal Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8da2a78-6b7f-53b8-bffd-d448c3f847ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471239} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc7d23e-5f63-597f-b45f-ccd132f97e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bc7d23e-5f63-597f-b45f-ccd132f97e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471240} :answer-field/id #uuid "17e335b8-b98e-50fa-a484-bdd5b2409741" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(y)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58586351-d58f-59e4-a4a4-9c608e02df09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471241} {:answer/id #uuid "6db9990c-720e-51d7-bb30-d39dacae1573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58586351-d58f-59e4-a4a4-9c608e02df09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471241} :answer-field/id #uuid "65c3c397-0d1d-516b-ac99-7fe8b9c00f19" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(y)$ is ${R}_{0}^{+}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472126} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2441682b-b895-530a-8549-bac4919a1d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471243} {:answer/id #uuid "afd5bf33-6d41-5522-b11a-167be7a2855e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2441682b-b895-530a-8549-bac4919a1d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471243} :answer-field/id #uuid "234c4b97-1890-58ba-9c35-cecd4649c7c3" :answer-field/key "$∀y\\in {R}_{0}^{+},\\,P(y).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1dd2623-6f10-56c3-88a0-4d1c15254f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-183501" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(y):$ ${y}^{3}\\ge 0$ and ${y}^{2}<0.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set ${R}_{0}^{+},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *universal quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true on the entire universal set $U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate coincides with the universal set $U:$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=U\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"${y}^{3}\\ge 0$\" is ${R}_{0}^{+},$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"${y}^{2}<0$\" is $∅.$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={R}_{0}^{+}\\cap ∅=∅.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(y)$ is $∅.$” is true. The truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(y)$ is ${R}_{0}^{+}.$” is false. Indeed, ${T}_{P}\\ne {R}_{0}^{+}.$\n\n- Statement $∀y\\in {R}_{0}^{+},\\,P(y).$ is false. Since ${T}_{P}$ does *not* coincide with the universal set, the statement $∀y\\in R,\\,P(y)$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(y)$ is $∅.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114dedd9-ed3d-5d25-8616-030ea4bd84c9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Universal Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "defba699-4a25-5079-8da7-191e906362c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471245} {:answer/id #uuid "2ae74a0e-8685-51b9-8b86-3ea38abb603b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "defba699-4a25-5079-8da7-191e906362c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471245} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa65fd8b-9a17-5a0f-94a1-cbfbb0757ec1" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6253e5dd-f178-507e-b0cb-82fbbd44aa21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471247} {:answer/id #uuid "c1539409-9db3-5470-a898-4ac923e6605f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1539409-9db3-5470-a898-4ac923e6605f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471248} :answer-field/id #uuid "c22a0b36-aaab-5d47-a469-7b5766b9a356" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba0e68d6-a9b0-5205-8fe6-9f651cd5ce63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471249} {:answer/id #uuid "b2b3038d-718e-582d-9c3c-f62a5783d2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2b3038d-718e-582d-9c3c-f62a5783d2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471250} :answer-field/id #uuid "646129fd-784c-5a2c-b410-5c53d3b646ed" :answer-field/key "$∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df50f5a8-2783-58fd-a4cd-90489ec7d8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-183505" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x>0$ or $x\\le 0.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *universal quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true on the entire universal set $U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate coincides with the universal set $U:$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=U\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$x>0$\" is ${Z}^{+},$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"$x\\le 0$\" is ${Z}_{0}^{-}.$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={Z}^{+}\\cup {Z}_{0}^{-}=Z.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=Z.$\n\n- Statement $∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ coincides with the universal set, the statement $∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$”; $∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114dedd9-ed3d-5d25-8616-030ea4bd84c9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Universal Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cba4701d-2fd6-5372-b880-8d434ccdb270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471251} {:answer/id #uuid "446db8d7-7cb7-5377-b9b2-bacbb4007a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "446db8d7-7cb7-5377-b9b2-bacbb4007a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471252} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d008faa-d8bb-541b-9843-da1781408cfe" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(z)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf171081-1331-5db9-a2de-12b23429df59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471253} {:answer/id #uuid "d3528246-9536-5d23-b342-adba8ac5dab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf171081-1331-5db9-a2de-12b23429df59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471253} :answer-field/id #uuid "82ab5c53-5e15-5ea1-b774-b6f68e133cf3" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(z)$ is $R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472132} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8b3a8c0-a6c1-578d-9257-3e5ed98ce4ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471255} {:answer/id #uuid "9bc632e2-76b4-5b92-9ae0-3c66fa0e0b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8b3a8c0-a6c1-578d-9257-3e5ed98ce4ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471255} :answer-field/id #uuid "78d00a60-493e-5993-9de4-453b1082e9fc" :answer-field/key "$∀z\\in R,\\,P(z).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9947189b-8991-5f0c-ad01-e90d4c094369" :question/math-academy-id "q-183507" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(z):$ ${e}^{z}<0$ or ${z}^{4}\\le -1.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $R,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *universal quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true on the entire universal set $U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate coincides with the universal set $U:$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=U\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"${e}^{z}<0$\" is $∅,$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"${z}^{4}\\le -1$\" is $∅.$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=∅\\cup ∅=∅.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(z)$ is $∅.$” is true. The truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(z)$ is $R.$” is false. Indeed, ${T}_{P}\\ne R.$\n\n- Statement $∀z\\in R,\\,P(z).$ is false. Since ${T}_{P}$ does *not* coincide with the universal set, the statement $∀z\\in R,\\,P(z)$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(z)$ is $∅.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114dedd9-ed3d-5d25-8616-030ea4bd84c9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Universal Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18ae95b