17592186471262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57a82495-a59e-5851-b7b5-f73ae72ff17d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471262} :answer-field/id #uuid "35a4aa85-26f8-5790-8558-316e6fcb8d17" :answer-field/key "$∀z\\in Q,\\,P(z).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "53e303c8-88d9-51db-bc34-ac5638b42f29" :question/math-academy-id "q-183511" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(z):$ $\\frac{z}{2}\\in Q⇒(z+1)^{2}\\ge 0.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Q,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *universal quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true on the entire universal set $U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate coincides with the universal set $U:$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=U\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$\\frac{z}{2}\\in Q$\" is $Q,$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"$(z+1)^{2}\\ge 0$\" is $Q.$\n\nSince $A⇒B≡¬A∨B,$ the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\overset{―}{Q}\\cup Q=∅\\cup Q=Q.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(z)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is not empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(z)$ is $Q.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=Q.$\n\n- Statement $∀z\\in Q,\\,P(z).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ coincides with the universal set, the statement $∀z\\in Q,\\,P(z)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(z)$ is $Q.$”; $∀z\\in Q,\\,P(z).$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99e8deea-e8f4-5ff7-bd37-2da11ae10889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471263} {:answer/id #uuid "7cba0954-6700-5c1a-b3a9-0533c67f4a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cba0954-6700-5c1a-b3a9-0533c67f4a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471264} :answer-field/id #uuid "905855c6-d163-536a-ad9f-e392902c0e00" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(z)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "802fa2ed-3e2a-5dc8-9bd4-3cc9b95510ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471265} {:answer/id #uuid "5759a99b-eb18-5f4b-8146-b27b89d56c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "802fa2ed-3e2a-5dc8-9bd4-3cc9b95510ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471265} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c260fb3-24b1-5e74-8cf9-41a7e45f67e4" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(z)$ is $N.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55f3de