alse.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(z)$ is $∅.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cad0ba93-8091-533c-a25a-a5d7cfbae973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471269} {:answer/id #uuid "58928286-7dc1-5197-b088-818d869c772e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad0ba93-8091-533c-a25a-a5d7cfbae973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471269} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7842b45-92cd-5a9d-80f0-68486f8068bc" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1208e82-0729-505c-90d5-2ea36adad969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471271} {:answer/id #uuid "856332bc-5b98-5598-b36e-d06b239ce7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "856332bc-5b98-5598-b36e-d06b239ce7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471272} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdb1233e-b724-550d-9b84-7a512bda69ea" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b0d93c4-ca3f-54a1-9887-9ce986e0bba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471273} {:answer/id #uuid "86b14e15-bf92-5a92-b243-e5fd660adda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b14e15-bf92-5a92-b243-e5fd660adda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471274} :answer-field/id #uuid "519c14e9-cdb2-5e83-a514-295e0a236ed8" :answer-field/key "$∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f36cab2-ae5b-5390-a225-e9d92c28352a" :question/math-academy-id "q-183554" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{3}<0$ or ${x}^{2}=0$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set ${Z}^{-},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"${x}^{3}<0$\" is the set ${Z}^{-},$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"${x}^{2}=0$\" is $∅.$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={Z}^{-}\\cup ∅={Z}^{-}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}={Z}^{-}.$\n\n- Statement $∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is *not* empty, the statement $∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(x)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$”; $∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x).$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822864b0-d4f3-5454-af92-71c3600dc845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471275} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca96f6e-9734-506e-9a01-9c7094e585f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822864b0-d4f3-5454-af92-71c3600dc845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471275} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bdad168-d730-54bd-a2f5-90e6a40c8c4d" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd50b686-9088-5e8e-9480-616099180f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471277} {:answer/id #uuid "08f6ec98-4ea0-5d97-94e5-7fc31474e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08f6ec98-4ea0-5d97-94e5-7fc31474e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471278} :answer-field/id #uuid "185a34c6-5872-513c-806d-314d0b02664a" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bbc8f4a-60f3-5fff-9e49-e1ecb34e09db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471279} {:answer/id #uuid "9d04b366-0c6a-52bd-b794-28707736ff32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d04b366-0c6a-52bd-b794-28707736ff32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471280} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7e29fa1-6323-54f9-ac16-2c9f9af53123" :answer-field/key "$∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "79e978ef-4c7c-5a72-a1cc-3c8d675edfbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-183559" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}-2=0⇒{x}^{2}\\in N$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$\\sqrt{x}-2=0$\" is the set ${4},$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"${x}^{2}\\in N$\" is $Z∖{0}.$\n\nSince $A⇒B≡¬A∨B,$ the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\overset{―}{{4}}\\cup (Z∖{0})=(Z∖{4})\\cup (Z∖{0})=Z.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=Z.$\n\n- Statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is *not* empty, the statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$”; $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9d0b4f3-89cc-5718-9b99-3608b198a961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471281} {:answer/id #uuid "37313c70-39b7-5dc9-b3c4-a19acf370901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d0b4f3-89cc-5718-9b99-3608b198a961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471281} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43f4f46-1ff7-5a5f-b67a-a7033ebb99e9" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472146} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e7b892-0684-5b9b-b9b2-a3f62c816e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471283} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ca0b4c-5971-598e-b066-6bedf819e07d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03e7b892-0684-5b9b-b9b2-a3f62c816e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471283} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe01474-e943-5480-b617-9630e94ff1a0" :answer-field/key "The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)$ is $R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a3cdfb-8bb9-54ae-8804-4c4f876ac849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471285} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fce173-02a3-518a-95ef-ae472714bf66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a3cdfb-8bb9-54ae-8804-4c4f876ac849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471285} :answer-field/id #uuid "24f5bbf3-595e-55dd-8c22-bb49db12000e" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44159662-1bf3-5bee-9ce6-75e394e9c1e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-183586" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R$ and $y\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\n$$\n\nfrom option $∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ For all reals $x$ and $y,$ we have $\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R.$ is false since $\\sqrt{2y}\\in R$ is not true for some real $y.$ Say, for $y=-1.$\n\n- Statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)$ is $R.$” is false. For the predicate\n\n$$\nP(x):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\n$$\n\nwe note that $P(x)$ is false for all values $x\\in R.$ For example, \n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{y}\\in R\n$$\n\nis false, since we can take $y=-1.$ Similarly,\n\n$$\nP(2):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R\n$$\n\nis false, since we can take $y=-2.$ In general, it's sufficient to take $y=-x$ for any value of $x.$\n\n- Statement $∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$ is false. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)\n$$\n\n \ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in R\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R}_{P(x)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(x)$ is true over the universal set $R.$ But, according to statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)$ is $R.$”, this is not the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1cd21af-f2fc-5f66-997a-4e2c91258940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471287} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f18e7d-fdb8-53fe-8f50-eaaac3ed1598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1cd21af-f2fc-5f66-997a-4e2c91258940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471287} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ed5ac1a-9b04-5b9c-be9d-47fe1e8d63d8" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,\\,2y=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba4a2deb-40ce-5aff-a38b-c2d9900b7006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471289} {:answer/id #uuid "443319b0-9a52-570e-9382-2ad4c166bcd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba4a2deb-40ce-5aff-a38b-c2d9900b7006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471289} :answer-field/id #uuid "e823795e-dd00-51ef-b876-a9f7aa0d9ea5" :answer-field/key "The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbba717-65e5-566d-8fd3-783fb2ce62b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471291} {:answer/id #uuid "abb18620-d583-5cb5-bb83-c3e2a178cf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb18620-d583-5cb5-bb83-c3e2a178cf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471292} :answer-field/id #uuid "a75d0c30-1919-56dd-97c7-3982426fe9c7" :answer-field/key "$∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "391922f6-f189-52a8-9bf4-83a4fbad32e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-183598" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R$ and $y\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\n$$\n\nfrom option $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a real $x$ such that, for every real $y,$ we have $xy=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $∀\\,y\\in R,\\,2y=0.$ is false since $2y=0$ is not true for some real $y.$ Say, for $y=1.$\n\n- Statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)$ is $∅.$” is false.  The predicate\n\n$$\nP(x):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,xy=0\n$$\n\nis true for some $x\\in R.$ For example, \n\n$$\nP(0):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,0\\cdot y=0\n$$\n\nis true. Therefore, its truth set is not empty.\n\n- Statement $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$ is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0}_{P(x)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(x)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)$ is $∅.$”, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a04d1c6-5fef-5eb1-b8a0-6e8d2bc0cb0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471353} {:answer/id #uuid "28dd7535-fa0f-594a-badb-bbba90cf96c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28dd7535-fa0f-594a-badb-bbba90cf96c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471354} :answer-field/id #uuid "39dda0b1-b1e4-5398-90a6-9476fff2abd4" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9546767-c4b3-57a2-b994-f01725c8569f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471355} {:answer/id #uuid "c9abd13e-9f4d-567b-bbf2-70e8c2cc7a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9546767-c4b3-57a2-b994-f01725c8569f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471355} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd300e54-475d-59cb-b72c-6f2553db14b3" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2624e8-195a-5c38-b473-4ece34824be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471357} {:answer/id #uuid "e0091fd0-01af-5579-805f-bdd3dda2655a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e2624e8-195a-5c38-b473-4ece34824be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471357} :answer-field/id #uuid "d218648f-439f-5a95-ad9a-80f155bba199" :answer-field/key "$∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a35352a2-6307-508d-9bf3-f6a84812f3f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-216492" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $2x+1=0$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the solution of the equation $2x+1=0$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ but this solution doesn't belong to the universal set. Therefore, the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=∅.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is true. The truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$” is false.\n\n- Statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ is false. Since ${T}_{P}$ is empty, the statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc5affe6-4770-5548-9507-5c89a64c9b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471561} {:answer/id #uuid "dde18b4b-8640-5ed9-92a5-b12e63fff964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dde18b4b-8640-5ed9-92a5-b12e63fff964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471562} :answer-field/id #uuid "320576ab-882c-5a79-b3a3-b28f006e057e" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472286} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93698920-d848-54df-841c-dab3e524be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471563} {:answer/id #uuid "096b59d8-3cb6-5a1b-b69d-9f2da2407523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93698920-d848-54df-841c-dab3e524be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471563} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b2efca-871f-5c8a-891c-318bab239316" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bb77a49-0313-5979-a239-3449474b79f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471565} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b30ce9-1264-57ec-9dd7-435dcd422034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb77a49-0313-5979-a239-3449474b79f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471565} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2e21158-0876-5654-b53e-3a157ac915f2" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **onto**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8bf28a0-bd57-55ca-8858-3f8b81db61da" :question/math-academy-id "q-80019" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}+1?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/be/bed7b280998fe987276ca5820b987f672404d52d00f532db819db1166118ed70.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$  in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$” is true. From the graph, the lowest $y$-value is $1,$ and it occurs at the point $(2,1).$ The graph will cover all $y$-values from $y=1$ and greater, including the number $1,$ so the range of the function is $[1,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false. Consider $y=0.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **onto**” is false. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b406b689-3c74-5395-adad-002234ac8699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471657} {:answer/id #uuid "317451ef-f89e-5251-a9e3-a76136ab46fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "317451ef-f89e-5251-a9e3-a76136ab46fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471658} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d48b900-e4e0-5b60-897f-7050febe69c7" :answer-field/key "$¬(¬A∨¬B)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed3c720f-f39d-5b54-8fff-3b1de6263fb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471659} {:answer/id #uuid "341e88e4-f3fe-58f3-8ec1-ebde1c717286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "341e88e4-f3fe-58f3-8ec1-ebde1c717286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471660} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e88922e-58b5-569b-a8b4-fb942b9c3a45" :answer-field/key "$A∧B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec04081c-be9d-57b9-836b-b15362aa3a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471661} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a1bd1-1966-5f8c-93f4-2ac284a874e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec04081c-be9d-57b9-836b-b15362aa3a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471661} :answer-field/id #uuid "94e63a8b-40e6-5937-baa4-a71931a1c8d8" :answer-field/key "$A∨B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1094e86-e368-5edf-a0b9-d55c19636e6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81485" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬A∨¬B)\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬(¬A∨¬B)$ and $A∧B$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬(¬A∨¬B)$; $A∧B$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "382a6db7-2708-5711-885e-6f3f3037e8df" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Functions is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "320d9242-a62e-5c01-9167-d38710e9024c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471809} {:answer/id #uuid "362b3fdd-9f80-5650-bbde-24dd702199b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "362b3fdd-9f80-5650-bbde-24dd702199b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471810} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd6540a6-001f-53ab-803a-662d03037eca" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472410} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8138994-dcf1-5ca7-b1d2-22437449679c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471811} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4bef01-6686-5bbb-b4b9-e6d742a886ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8138994-dcf1-5ca7-b1d2-22437449679c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471811} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ac12782-25b8-5598-a320-1aba893cb274" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472411} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15dc53de-e750-5228-914a-e0782ec8491a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471813} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d30f76-9cdf-5b19-82fb-3fe455865e34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15dc53de-e750-5228-914a-e0782ec8491a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471813} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f2dcce-48f9-5c4f-8b06-c72964cad539" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0457d3f-7a7d-578e-b127-39bac9e28900" :question/math-academy-id "q-99863" :question/problem "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,{f}_{3}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[-\\pi /2,\\pi /2]$ of continuous functions over $[-\\pi /2,\\pi /2]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is called orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩=⟨t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the integration by parts formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2}){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )}{2}-\\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )}{2})+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}{4}{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =0+(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )}{4}) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{3}(t)⟩=⟨t,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the integration by parts formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}+{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-(-\\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =0+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)) \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =2\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{3}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "382a6db7-2708-5711-885e-6f3f3037e8df" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Functions is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb3f792-8daa-5481-90a3-72c22e1e0cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471815} {:answer/id #uuid "37bf6595-efed-5e05-9eea-c39ccace55ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bb3f792-8daa-5481-90a3-72c22e1e0cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471815} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef3c0786-1837-57ae-b61a-5fcc2a1ae0da" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472413} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82d9a59f-6071-55e9-ba83-81a93266ba78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471817} {:answer/id #uuid "7f4ccf74-dfd0-5457-ae1d-2f4b1376f55f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4ccf74-dfd0-5457-ae1d-2f4b1376f55f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471818} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4772d99-ef37-508b-be2b-5bf2236274df" :answer-field/key "${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472414} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "983ffe32-ea8e-5549-a804-3f8a808db229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471819} {:answer/id #uuid "9b9010c5-b935-59a9-aa88-3c4656c8a125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "983ffe32-ea8e-5549-a804-3f8a808db229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471819} :answer-field/id #uuid "9241636c-59e4-57aa-90d4-9f47ca3f6f1e" :answer-field/key "$S={{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "866dfd7d-0156-5915-b7a2-48bb304694df" :question/math-academy-id "q-99949" :question/problem "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{f}_{3}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[-\\pi /2,\\pi /2]$ of continuous functions over $[-\\pi /2,\\pi /2]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is called orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the identity $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{4}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)⟩=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ differentiating we have $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S={{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee9c51fe-1f93-5f07-8dfb-54553964dbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470775} {:answer/id #uuid "be8844ed-55c4-59b2-b7f6-dbf5de4e307e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9c51fe-1f93-5f07-8dfb-54553964dbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470775} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6115a53-5892-5b95-b119-f5eb572d5212" :answer-field/key "$f(-2)\\ne f(2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8a1014a-6170-583a-a39e-d8ba72176fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470777} {:answer/id #uuid "176a2196-a6d5-5fb9-84b6-11cad8e38f0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8a1014a-6170-583a-a39e-d8ba72176fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470777} :answer-field/id #uuid "2641bae7-0817-5b22-9386-7370addc7324" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de4b935-368e-5457-a4f8-db8dfd1a7594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470779} {:answer/id #uuid "b7dab165-506c-51cc-b247-9891d757f656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7dab165-506c-51cc-b247-9891d757f656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470780} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e8260e3-2830-52f4-92c1-0a618d01500a" :answer-field/key "$f$ is not an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41a4e16b-532b-5af9-a855-bdbc2ac881f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-105203" :question/problem "![](images/64/64b81ef8b99a70ae69b607b9c9440e9588576f8ea2243a8aa82f52d92bde8630.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,2]\\to [-1,5]$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-2)\\ne f(2)$ is false. According to the graph, we have $f(-2)=f(2)=5.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false. Again, we have $f(-2)=f(2)$ but $-2\\ne 2.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is not an injection” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false, $f$ is not an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is not an injection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eace52b-7e6e-5ec8-b519-3c4941f46c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470787} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb5d57f-63a6-5a6d-8168-fb5fce1121eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bb5d57f-63a6-5a6d-8168-fb5fce1121eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470788} :answer-field/id #uuid "b953bfa5-4a49-5115-8695-97ca60313935" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b678175d-5703-57e2-a818-f6453b55fa13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470789} {:answer/id #uuid "d274bcce-f637-54a1-a37c-89d6ebd6489b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d274bcce-f637-54a1-a37c-89d6ebd6489b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470790} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1779ddf-7824-52f2-a5da-31f0049c6613" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471900} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfbc10a7-9ed9-50ea-a8d4-7fb24bb1cdb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470791} {:answer/id #uuid "515b6786-c3f0-596c-984e-79d5fc618129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "515b6786-c3f0-596c-984e-79d5fc618129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470792} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c02af87-593e-51e0-bb13-98a4fee0c423" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db660bb9-e18a-5aa6-8b12-2d9637cff073" :question/math-academy-id "q-105224" :question/problem "![](images/32/32957c5f0b4eeb76253f9fe812e2025b93a2cd5c65870f5a0b3608ce545dd4c5.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is true. Indeed, according to the diagram, for every element $y\\in Y,$ we have an arrow from some element $x\\in X$ to it, which means that $f(x)=y.$ So, $f$ is a surjection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a bijection” is true. Indeed, since both statements “$f$ is a surjection” and “$f$ is an injection” are true, $f$ is a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is a surjection”; “$f$ is an injection”; “$f$ is a bijection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fbd78fe-5ede-5795-9622-962461ceaffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470823} {:answer/id #uuid "9de6e2bf-f8e9-549b-9aed-e689c26328e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fbd78fe-5ede-5795-9622-962461ceaffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470823} :answer-field/id #uuid "3837b8ab-5872-5992-97f4-40787670506a" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca534b3e-7b8d-50f0-8361-4fe1356e93d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470825} {:answer/id #uuid "d603d976-e8c8-5eb2-8c88-cea3ab366fdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca534b3e-7b8d-50f0-8361-4fe1356e93d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470825} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4e0316e-a490-5722-a171-17b4936ef2c1" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471918} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c5d5dc3-30a6-556f-a142-ba2a5ab13561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470827} {:answer/id #uuid "551313b9-9c31-565f-bd3f-853edba26752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c5d5dc3-30a6-556f-a142-ba2a5ab13561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470827} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f1b659c-be5a-5301-b7ea-21955cb2e5fa" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea34001e-7666-5760-9335-3a797f196771" :question/math-academy-id "q-105330" :question/problem "![](images/88/8845d8cc2664c92637e06961f1d5c17b98afcb72470d1463fbd58aaf5691ca4c.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=(x+1)^{2}-2$, which of the following statements are true?  \n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. There are horizontal lines (such as the one depicted below) that cross the graph of $f(x)$ more than once.\n\n![](images/d6/d6b2a99811341aa07bc3e91df973504fad57ac4a71a38406707b5d311247d61d.png)\n\n        \n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. For example, there is not $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-4.$ So, $f$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false, because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98db4bdf-35c0-572f-a8d0-dd5af5d2d797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471045} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5b1cde-3a17-5c26-ae0b-684c07d6c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e5b1cde-3a17-5c26-ae0b-684c07d6c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471046} :answer-field/id #uuid "28b9829d-7120-5b5c-92bd-c1ef0c0e2fa6" :answer-field/key "$P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472028} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9127507d-cd00-5560-bb89-a83a30f508fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471047} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4074bd-8e93-5f12-a606-f60e237bc602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9127507d-cd00-5560-bb89-a83a30f508fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471047} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbaf59b-eeb3-51ce-8a01-5dc52517e99d" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472029} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf59bd71-a0bd-5b9f-a650-5a3684e0a341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471049} {:answer/id #uuid "ee3117e1-426e-540f-a519-e302a751ae0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf59bd71-a0bd-5b9f-a650-5a3684e0a341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471049} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d335f5-b08f-5856-be51-b11cb49c2f5f" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5449cbef-825d-5bac-be24-822940400b4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-143335" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=2,Y=2)=f(2,2)=0.2.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.5\\cdot 0.4=0.2.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Taking $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =0.1\\ne 0.2\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198400 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4179839d-85c4-5325-9293-e332bd209597" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Inverse Function Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dfbfd1f-8c57-5fbe-a046-ceb729aa8a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471131} {:answer/id #uuid "73106404-c5ab-5410-828f-e3512801d032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dfbfd1f-8c57-5fbe-a046-ceb729aa8a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471131} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff7b3c6d-8c28-54e5-9c3d-44c52e635b0b" :answer-field/key "The function $f$ is invertible on $U.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8d21e81-e466-5275-b6d7-e8596ffd6af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471133} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea8393e-8b7e-5757-8a39-9abbd88090d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8d21e81-e466-5275-b6d7-e8596ffd6af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471133} :answer-field/id #uuid "8576233d-a2de-53f9-8fb3-a010c3910212" :answer-field/key "The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable on $U.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c413dcb0-496c-5788-83c8-a5743c676e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471135} {:answer/id #uuid "490e1529-0fed-5e20-985c-3761de5fd52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490e1529-0fed-5e20-985c-3761de5fd52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471136} :answer-field/id #uuid "885433fd-1178-5da3-bd21-57f732fa2bb4" :answer-field/key "The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4dcab08e-c33d-5c73-a45a-265b0e425858" :question/math-academy-id "q-161847" :question/problem "Let $f:U\\to R$ be continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R$ such that $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U.$ Which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The function $f$ is invertible on $U.$” is false. According to the theorem, the function $f$ must be invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$ which could be smaller than $U.$ \n\nFor example, the function $f(x)=2{x}^{4}$ satisfies the conditions of the inverse function theorem for $U=(-2,2)$ and $a=-1.$ However, $f(x)$ is not invertible on the entire set $U,$ only on a subset of $U.$\n\n- Statement “The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable on $U.$” is false. According to the theorem, the function${f}^{-1}$ must be continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ which could be smaller than $U.$\n\n- Statement “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$” is true. According to the theorem, we must have ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229161 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "151add00-204f-5795-aff9-cceddc26b24b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Other Methods"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ac012a3-2b7a-5fad-8266-cc29057d1a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471411} {:answer/id #uuid "abb54835-096e-58c4-9110-0c96b1602e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb54835-096e-58c4-9110-0c96b1602e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471412} :answer-field/id #uuid "baf6dcb7-aa48-5618-82dc-14ac46166291" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=0.1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472211} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b402935f-58a9-5752-addc-960e5ce215cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471413} {:answer/id #uuid "895c8e8e-e7d7-5a94-aafc-1059169056b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895c8e8e-e7d7-5a94-aafc-1059169056b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471414} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae7169b-c55d-542d-8b6e-fb38683fad9c" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=0.8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00902814-4c4b-5e69-95a4-aabb29cc9517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471415} {:answer/id #uuid "36f94c4d-bb31-5998-9936-bc54616e115a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36f94c4d-bb31-5998-9936-bc54616e115a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471416} :answer-field/id #uuid "847bc4cf-85e6-5570-86a1-1732fb6b1d8a" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=1.2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5c47e6e-a2a4-5e7d-b62c-f7e727ef436a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471417} {:answer/id #uuid "903f2c91-49ea-5190-8870-540dc5840c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "903f2c91-49ea-5190-8870-540dc5840c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471418} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f00f93a-d100-582b-98a8-1e7e4c8bdb03" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7019503-fd19-5657-a7e0-238936f56d67" :question/math-academy-id "q-334241" :question/problem "For which of the following values is the implicit Euler method stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the implicit Euler method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method \n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the implicit Euler method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the implicit Euler Method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.1)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.1}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.1}| \\\\  & =0.9090…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.8)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.8}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.8}| \\\\  & =0.5555…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.2)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+1.2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{2.2}| \\\\  & =0.4545…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(5)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+5}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{6}| \\\\  & =0.1666…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\lambda Δx=0.1$; $\\lambda Δx=0.8$; $\\lambda Δx=1.2$; $\\lambda Δx=5$.\n\nNote that, since the implicit Euler method is absolutely stable, it is stable for all possible values of $\\lambda Δx.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cec6272-e3c1-5d79-8e5f-cb77ba066b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471615} {:answer/id #uuid "59363834-1ac9-5e0d-9623-b9bdf850fa57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cec6272-e3c1-5d79-8e5f-cb77ba066b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471615} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c8166f1-6fe1-57a1-9c84-1d90e80859df" :answer-field/key "$f(-2)\\ne f(1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f98ee01d-c506-56f5-b241-ee8d6979bf62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471617} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f29d7b-ddc2-512a-884a-f31bc704d36f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f98ee01d-c506-56f5-b241-ee8d6979bf62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471617} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e346a9-d793-5487-abe6-bdec0eca1c88" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ed9cbc2-9dea-5d6b-9553-cdf98fc3d93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471619} {:answer/id #uuid "691c6242-9f3b-57a5-9a92-094e02607d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ed9cbc2-9dea-5d6b-9553-cdf98fc3d93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471619} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd29552-cf51-56f9-888e-09e014b8609f" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **one-to-one**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb0a5436-5069-574d-ac30-ea6987db593d" :question/math-academy-id "q-80376" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d81a4317d789968de29f34b42358d44e74c8bbe4717467a4c780beb633dc0d5.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-2)\\ne f(1)$ is false. According to the graph, we have $f(-2)=f(1)=-1.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false. Again, we have $f(-2)=f(1)$ but $-2\\ne 1.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **one-to-one**” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6537425a-3a23-527c-9da5-df969a886b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471621} {:answer/id #uuid "70384b8d-3049-593c-bffc-f225d07ff798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70384b8d-3049-593c-bffc-f225d07ff798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471622} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1968b7-411d-5d23-b491-bba506874af9" :answer-field/key "$f(1)\\ne f(2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "620220df-3c93-5179-9f74-25ff459cd253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471623} {:answer/id #uuid "7d76c890-f63f-55f5-8bfb-96b40fc2d65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d76c890-f63f-55f5-8bfb-96b40fc2d65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471624} :answer-field/id #uuid "4aa74849-6ed3-5eb6-ace4-7fa1690bd44b" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36719e80-3e96-5b3d-8c80-f87abb5ce103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471625} {:answer/id #uuid "62ce85e1-7d09-54c4-a2a7-9d8e38606dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62ce85e1-7d09-54c4-a2a7-9d8e38606dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471626} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b46a5ab-4a37-5bc8-a5b2-54d266daa89c" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **one-to-one**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5a04c07f-9732-5fba-9678-462e7c23fd4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80387" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[1,\\infty )\\to [0,\\infty )$ which is given by $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/ae/aeda30e69b9bc433e5f345822d4221e194981ce132a022f28632814376c5910e.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(1)\\ne f(2)$ is true. We have $f(1)=(1-1)^{2}=0$ and $f(2)=(2-1)^{2}=1.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[1,\\infty )$ that map to the same element in $[0,\\infty ).$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **one-to-one**” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(1)\\ne f(2)$; “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$”; “$f$ is **one-to-one**”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de15b416-0988-5682-8b4c-df22f0bdeba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471705} {:answer/id #uuid "bed38b8f-cd64-5808-97db-78c92453dfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de15b416-0988-5682-8b4c-df22f0bdeba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471705} :answer-field/id #uuid "12862809-b36b-5719-ad7e-aab5ef076094" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "636183c1-9b92-5010-925f-bf2aeb0bf21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471707} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7e8dc-e348-599b-9e93-a55b371e6734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7e8dc-e348-599b-9e93-a55b371e6734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471708} :answer-field/id #uuid "e96b1a9f-58a9-5646-8df6-c11742da070a" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61e2d736-eecc-5dde-8872-cf1f75f92c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471709} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5391a9-7a0c-59b9-9fa7-c293bd935ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61e2d736-eecc-5dde-8872-cf1f75f92c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471709} :answer-field/id #uuid "f35689a1-265b-5ad7-8923-1155ca2a938d" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e966053-1b79-5d5f-9b9a-6962c445b14d" :question/math-academy-id "q-82293" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd6de23e9b33d0e86a91eb4bf6b81a9d443c1b389182f1c05bf10d048f0c0402.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. Consider $y=5.$ As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $5\\in Y.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* a surjection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a bijection” is false. Indeed, since statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false,  $f$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is an injection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242