er/id #uuid "eec2d395-740a-5cef-ac04-a21b8cf7a684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eec2d395-740a-5cef-ac04-a21b8cf7a684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471716} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd2f7d7-d32f-52ad-b157-23fafe6b4b6d" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3819ae9-243b-5030-9bcc-f473557d3d03" :question/math-academy-id "q-82297" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bbe19e6a595d7b48e7f18382ed0a66452ba28c86925edad81a296cb7dd26a77f.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is true. Indeed, according to the diagram, for every element $y\\in Y,$ we have an arrow from some element $x\\in X$ to it, which means that $f(x)=y.$ So, $f$ is a surjection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a bijection” is true. Indeed, since both statements “$f$ is a surjection” and “$f$ is an injection” are true, $f$ is a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is a surjection”; “$f$ is an injection”; “$f$ is a bijection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f5a15ef-9aac-5edc-8478-bfff007cdfd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471717} {:answer/id #uuid "8322b784-b416-5f2c-bfb8-2580815fc7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f5a15ef-9aac-5edc-8478-bfff007cdfd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471717} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca609a76-06c8-52db-8581-bd5c3848e1f6" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aee82d31-5b7a-5582-a21b-2fa920919744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471719} {:answer/id #uuid "3b0099d8-c719-5963-a690-03e8e902693a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aee82d31-5b7a-5582-a21b-2fa920919744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471719} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c020536-4c05-52fe-a219-595565574cf0" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5caacba0-5907-578d-8806-41c31bfd65ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471721} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6c6ef8-4b43-5a6a-ad55-0aa584b65ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5caacba0-5907-578d-8806-41c31bfd65ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471721} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7d9db8e-6447-574c-a155-456b3f1f55a7" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da5d5f20-c614-5648-b2cd-38bf72010ec2" :question/math-academy-id "q-82314" :question/problem "![](images/12/126abe41ac185c082d8cc28628e2db4b2708dd84ba351718184d949ddf582d3c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. Consider $y=2.$ As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $2\\in Y.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* a surjection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is false. We have $f(1)=f(4)$ but $1\\ne 4.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* an injection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a bijection” is false. Indeed, since statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false (as well as statement “$f$ is an injection”), $f$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8921441-1dc4-5449-aacb-e1ab5bc13f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471723} {:answer/id #uuid "623e141a-1cbf-55c1-8dbd-d594b76a28d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8921441-1dc4-5449-aacb-e1ab5bc13f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471723} :answer-field/id #uuid "577e30c4-9496-58ff-bd73-fb5da086efb0" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da7e484-02af-5597-b1fd-da3b8176ebd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471725} {:answer/id #uuid "27e78f90-3fd0-5f93-8b4a-141561c450e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da7e484-02af-5597-b1fd-da3b8176ebd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471725} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffdb055f-fba7-53d5-b7b3-3316bc59ab59" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472368} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3102ac0-d1e5-5474-bfac-ad06557b03a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471727} {:answer/id #uuid "195ad897-7a48-5a52-a5b1-f9353b04ade4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3102ac0-d1e5-5474-bfac-ad06557b03a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471727} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfaefc0f-ab90-5d24-983f-2d76b9e850dd" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24770296-d90b-538e-85f2-59d06d26123a" :question/math-academy-id "q-82317" :question/problem "For the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ which of the following  statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. For instance, $f(0)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )=f(2\\pi )$, but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$ So, $f(x)$ is not an injection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. For example, there is no $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=2.$ So, $f(x)$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bfbaec4-002f-56da-b603-ecb64b489280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471729} {:answer/id #uuid "ad13d9ab-3383-5fe3-ad9c-1c106572bb65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bfbaec4-002f-56da-b603-ecb64b489280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471729} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc29d875-c71c-520b-b763-2a953d8a8bac" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472370} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9720022a-1f68-56cc-99ed-1f884d93030f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471731} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7bbe52-574b-5d7b-b291-b264d3610735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9720022a-1f68-56cc-99ed-1f884d93030f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471731} :answer-field/id #uuid "4693e8e4-9ee4-5e25-ba31-16678f9c6ee2" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89adc61c-65db-5b4b-9356-e7f091e14040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471733} {:answer/id #uuid "1d8082f6-172b-5106-960f-2a9e83d9c98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89adc61c-65db-5b4b-9356-e7f091e14040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471733} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e3ba47-0ae4-55b9-8bcb-8639b038f4be" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3380502f-56f6-501e-b560-ed1186ab069f" :question/math-academy-id "q-82324" :question/problem "For the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{2}-1,$ which of the following  statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. For instance, $f(-1)=0=f(1)$, but $-1\\ne 1.$ So, $f(x)$ is not an injection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. For example, there is no $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-2.$ So, $f(x)$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c65cd4-8483-5860-b7e4-2e5f6999dce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470901} {:answer/id #uuid "d058bcfd-95da-5b43-97d7-abe7d98ec345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d058bcfd-95da-5b43-97d7-abe7d98ec345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470902} :answer-field/id #uuid "161e0852-2b45-54f8-8b42-267cc6b1c63c" :answer-field/key "$T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471956} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d386c399-9111-5bbd-9887-033eb7004c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470903} {:answer/id #uuid "69c4a485-5228-57d4-979a-ab95a231931b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69c4a485-5228-57d4-979a-ab95a231931b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470904} :answer-field/id #uuid "c48a1d31-3b71-53aa-a009-2fca300bedeb" :answer-field/key "$T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471957} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf59e0b8-6c9c-5268-9247-b6aa262b7519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470905} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2f1a31-c756-5d23-affa-6305848f8743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc2f1a31-c756-5d23-affa-6305848f8743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470906} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f7620bf-1e26-5a27-9705-fa63bd75423e" :answer-field/key "$T$ is a linear transformation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2b3861b-a381-5b7c-bc56-9232209a631c" :question/math-academy-id "q-12008" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x+y \\\\ 4x+3y\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}kx+ky \\\\ 4kx+3ky\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}x+y \\\\ 4x+3y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 4({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+3({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{y}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+3{y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}+3{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Vertical Asymptotes With Common Factors When the Denominator Has Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c2e0a46-a4ee-5819-bfd8-b6605a0d8094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439879} {:answer/id #uuid "e9369708-bcb2-5c13-a3f7-152ce020d3b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c2e0a46-a4ee-5819-bfd8-b6605a0d8094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439879} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3d5ff2-3ae3-5582-b549-bdcb6611dd13" :answer-field/key "$x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffb34ed7-9fe8-5948-babf-545c5e4e0736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439881} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d04f5d-ce83-59f2-88c7-83f4627e68e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffb34ed7-9fe8-5948-babf-545c5e4e0736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439881} :answer-field/id #uuid "012b94fc-d8bf-510d-a520-9dfc6c1811ab" :answer-field/key "$x=- \\sqrt{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f170be1-ffb8-592e-bb80-9f0195579084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439883} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba98035-0918-59db-93dd-e795d4f5ebd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f170be1-ffb8-592e-bb80-9f0195579084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439883} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c94165b-9d14-56fa-8e1c-3541dde89a56" :answer-field/key "$x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "547ea0a2-9056-5429-bd0f-633e68fa5943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439885} {:answer/id #uuid "1638a4a5-ff97-5f43-b834-d3d67a690eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "547ea0a2-9056-5429-bd0f-633e68fa5943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439885} :answer-field/id #uuid "d89178d8-8578-52ac-9dd9-ce525bf7df93" :answer-field/key "$x=\\sqrt{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440300} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "965e8857-7f8e-5f00-aa12-bd8820ca46e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439887} {:answer/id #uuid "f7855e38-b957-5e31-90eb-6ce83b7a223b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "965e8857-7f8e-5f00-aa12-bd8820ca46e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439887} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1222c91-f556-5bcf-9084-5d1456dda102" :answer-field/key "$x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d87d550-5004-5d22-b9a3-b2335e96082d" :question/math-academy-id "q-6913" :question/problem "Find all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ does not have any vertical asymptotes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396176 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f34066f-00d4-55b1-8d73-96ef234a63ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471627} {:answer/id #uuid "40aeb5d5-faee-5b7e-8df5-e870d6e9a6e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f34066f-00d4-55b1-8d73-96ef234a63ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471627} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ba3123-b0fe-5ec0-9a8d-2073c4afa0b4" :answer-field/key "$T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3317098d-cf9d-5045-941b-07580beb38db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471629} {:answer/id #uuid "cef4ff68-717a-544a-9ae5-83dfb3142903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3317098d-cf9d-5045-941b-07580beb38db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471629} :answer-field/id #uuid "75df2837-8fbd-5207-9ab7-c0c5f47ed8b5" :answer-field/key "$T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "839e484e-16dc-5c22-99f9-7b695e23ac7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471631} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f23ace-b866-586d-8acb-fe6dd49060d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9f23ace-b866-586d-8acb-fe6dd49060d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471632} :answer-field/id #uuid "64c08e3e-68be-5c0c-ab6e-798878cc578f" :answer-field/key "$T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "72a3fd90-5133-5a81-a0e8-33ac74b2d520" :question/math-academy-id "q-8049" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ kx\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement “$T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7e68721-1e8c-56a5-a25e-20d32a560654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470853} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a535ba-5cfa-5970-a938-26f3c594993d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3a535ba-5cfa-5970-a938-26f3c594993d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470854} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0257ee2-c864-5405-bc21-712dc76df852" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471932} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "775e5742-9972-51b8-b6af-ae4ade5ae9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470855} {:answer/id #uuid "9443b334-1f11-553a-95cf-10edf7a52a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9443b334-1f11-553a-95cf-10edf7a52a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470856} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ecf819d-ba3e-547e-9704-406e5e9b7d59" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e33e7564-1735-5427-9e70-60f44a0e5c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470857} {:answer/id #uuid "29445738-cbab-570a-85ae-1651b69dc6d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29445738-cbab-570a-85ae-1651b69dc6d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470858} :answer-field/id #uuid "80cc35c3-1dad-5d2d-a2b0-facf839095ec" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c07f2a41-0b84-51be-b671-ed8827d6cdfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109247" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5cd4afd-f5f1-5130-995d-ad232575ab59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470925} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb66342-fc86-5e57-9e67-259e20418f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5cd4afd-f5f1-5130-995d-ad232575ab59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470925} :answer-field/id #uuid "47a0d924-2e67-5931-a9bf-ad0e1167d1d9" :answer-field/key "$-5<-4<-2<0<4<6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca636607-c205-5a1f-ab6e-f93f3df9dd9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470927} {:answer/id #uuid "f5778b68-9032-556b-8a27-e3eb2a7ad2af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca636607-c205-5a1f-ab6e-f93f3df9dd9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470927} :answer-field/id #uuid "becba87c-7dc5-519c-99db-d0133f1eda87" :answer-field/key "${-3,3,5,6}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d435f6-a83a-5417-9e54-4ead82bee06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470929} {:answer/id #uuid "9db54e02-f5d3-54cc-8aad-f5717f7c0e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7d435f6-a83a-5417-9e54-4ead82bee06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470929} :answer-field/id #uuid "1233fbc7-3066-5abc-a1f6-f99def0b1fce" :answer-field/key "${-4,4,5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62099c6-5c34-55aa-ad1f-5500db9aeb0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122932" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-4,6]?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement $-5<-4<-2<0<4<6$ is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since $-5$ does not belong to $[-4,6].$\n\n- Statement ${-3,3,5,6}$ is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-4.$\n\n- Statement ${-4,4,5}$ is not a partition of  $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6].$\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59486814-0d8e-599a-bf0f-57dc550e7b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437330} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dce793-5565-5d7f-905d-7cd04e4d56ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59486814-0d8e-599a-bf0f-57dc550e7b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437330} :answer-field/id #uuid "a341d84b-92d9-5335-b0b9-fd13587dacad" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1].$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74c41ab1-5221-54d6-bfb2-b2d2b1a66a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437332} {:answer/id #uuid "79a66b2d-395b-5d7a-972b-1551475dda80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74c41ab1-5221-54d6-bfb2-b2d2b1a66a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437332} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d83191a-11eb-57de-8d9a-63c9eb52fa02" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$ is the maximum value of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e7478e7-5c82-57c4-9e23-eb0f7d938047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437334} {:answer/id #uuid "c4654fa4-c8d7-53b9-af56-adb9aeac3408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e7478e7-5c82-57c4-9e23-eb0f7d938047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437334} :answer-field/id #uuid "548cb375-8481-538b-9ce6-63f0f2d26906" :answer-field/key "$x=15\\pi $ is in the domain." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4383ecaa-1c57-5705-8853-cba2341fc9fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-103812" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ therefore the function doesn't have a maximum value. Hence, statements “The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1].$” and “$y=-1$ is the maximum value of the function” are both false.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement “$x=15\\pi $ is in the domain” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Vertical Asymptotes With Common Factors When the Denominator Has Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b695010-193a-5cbf-8437-deaea37d1e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439445} {:answer/id #uuid "c3eb42b0-64fa-57df-989d-34ad71b77544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b695010-193a-5cbf-8437-deaea37d1e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439445} :answer-field/id #uuid "a05fb1c2-71ab-5897-b477-b35b2b52f361" :answer-field/key "$x=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 1759218644