db/id #edb/ref 17592186439452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ce65c6-c9ad-50c2-b008-fca69d6b6025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439451} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a35fdf6-4ccf-52f4-a7be-125347104920" :answer-field/key "$x=\\sqrt{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0085fda-c140-5022-a903-4aa2d0060987" :question/math-academy-id "q-113554" :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}-6}{{x}^{4}-9}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}-6}{{x}^{4}-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({x}^{2}-3)}{({x}^{2}-3)({x}^{2}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{({x}^{2}-3)}}{\\cancel{({x}^{2}-3)}({x}^{2}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+3=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d14dbef-9a16-537e-a182-87fd6853e543" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Divergent Sequences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57570228-8466-52cb-a11f-f04e18706442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470931} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8642b5-04f8-5c37-a14b-aed7ee7a7659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57570228-8466-52cb-a11f-f04e18706442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470931} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ffa6fff-c4b5-5b71-b3d9-ad640d9a3224" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{5}}{2{n}^{5}-1}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471971} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5d09e71-31ad-54bf-8cea-1a8f785b490a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470933} {:answer/id #uuid "022b26c2-7d25-5b06-a964-476aa350c72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "022b26c2-7d25-5b06-a964-476aa350c72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470934} :answer-field/id #uuid "528c0afa-a7a6-540b-be79-d029b67039c3" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c6fcdbe-5b61-5426-9e91-ddd477fc741b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470935} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe5aeb4-873c-584e-ac06-a0748a68d7f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c6fcdbe-5b61-5426-9e91-ddd477fc741b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470935} :answer-field/id #uuid "e500961e-1c74-5a51-95f4-6ce13652944a" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n}=\\frac{5}{{n}^{6}}$ for $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4187c6ec-17d9-5b83-9a20-6aff01cc94de" :question/math-academy-id "q-123315" :question/problem "Which of the following sequences diverge?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each sequence in turn. We need to calculate the limit of each sequence as $n$ approaches infinity.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{5}}{2{n}^{5}-1}$ for $n\\ge 1$”,  the dominant term in the denominator is $2{n}^{5},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{5}}{2{n}^{5}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\left(\\frac{{n}^{5}}{{n}^{5}}\\right)}{(\\frac{2{n}^{5}}{{n}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{n}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{(2-\\frac{1}{{n}^{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}}$ for $n\\ge 1$”, the dominant term in the denominator is $-{n}^{4},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{n}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{{n}^{5}}{{n}^{4}})}{(\\frac{2}{{n}^{4}}-\\frac{{n}^{4}}{{n}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}}-n)}{(\\frac{2}{{n}^{4}}-1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{0-n}{0-1} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not exist, so the sequence diverges.\n\n- In sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{5}{{n}^{6}}$ for $n\\ge 1$”,  the limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{5}{{n}^{6}}=0.\n$$\n\nThe limit exists, so the sequence converges.\n\nIn conclusion, sequence “${a}_{n}=\\frac{n-{n}^{5}}{2-{n}^{4}}$ for $n\\ge 1$” diverges."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09fa0899-a3d2-584f-8cdd-a471f8cfd16b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Special Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4c4b6f3-a9d9-5370-8991-9303e65c3015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472550} {:answer/id #uuid "d564422c-47a5-5ab6-8593-71deb3c3cd69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4c4b6f3-a9d9-5370-8991-9303e65c3015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472550} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b5d220c-18b5-57e7-a90d-58d07571e262" :answer-field/key "$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8657c195-208d-54ba-8639-f23613e3b183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472552} {:answer/id #uuid "9a555d27-4f3f-5c78-ba86-d3dbf70f47af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8657c195-208d-54ba-8639-f23613e3b183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472552} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ea2960f-36ab-5c79-bcb0-d8d666e973a1" :answer-field/key "$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0bdef0e-9550-5f87-ab43-3dab5f492509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472554} {:answer/id #uuid "5ded35e1-51c9-575b-8ae1-105fd098c53b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0bdef0e-9550-5f87-ab43-3dab5f492509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472554} :answer-field/id #uuid "55893052-4f9b-5d44-8cc1-a03cc42802a9" :answer-field/key "$R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8674af78-bd5e-58b6-917b-e86f01702cc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-126222" :question/problem "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $P$ is *not* a diagonal matrix since it's not a square matrix.\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a diagonal matrix since it's not a square matrix.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. But some of the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are not zeros (for instance, ${r}_{31}=7\\ne 0$).\n\nTherefore, none of the given are diagonal matrices."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{