 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439753} :answer-field/id #uuid "9289e91e-6f0c-5a94-b1b0-b92d76ca8929" :answer-field/key "$x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "10e486fb-a153-567a-b122-83eab72817c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-39936" :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{4}-1}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{4}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{({x}^{2}-1)({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)(x+1)}}{\\cancel{(x-1)(x+1)}({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+1=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110587 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b834b64-9679-56c2-b5e9-ee26a54b5e13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values in the Domain of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e693f80-a3a3-551a-967f-182e4c12c493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473242} {:answer/id #uuid "8835e78e-1e62-57b6-80f9-3386641d53b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8835e78e-1e62-57b6-80f9-3386641d53b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473243} :answer-field/id #uuid "b008506d-0569-5fde-b5ee-4d41d0b9e621" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\pi }{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3cbec53-2d59-565e-b893-c292adacfe80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473244} {:answer/id #uuid "6e4314c8-4230-52e3-b4d0-9b138072dd6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e4314c8-4230-52e3-b4d0-9b138072dd6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473245} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd874f9f-fbb9-5d95-9beb-7cd7270d087a" :answer-field/key "$2\\pi $" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7253d679-fba9-5e01-97d4-bcd23f4862a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473246} {:answer/id #uuid "073f3921-d722-50e5-9ec5-665fc78cf09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "073f3921-d722-50e5-9ec5-665fc78cf09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473247} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7491322-bde6-59cd-93f9-07496e821155" :answer-field/key "$-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6b8e8196-034c-5c0d-b75d-8445d18467fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-70777" :question/problem "Which of the following values lies in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/68/6860bcf04c508b0abe795b9e1699163ac9495818f6427b338ac6bbe17774b2d8.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, all the given values are in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110588 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f045b43-4785-5989-8b5a-dcb8401d1bb3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Graph of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9c80853-3a87-5b9c-abfb-93f2d45941ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473248} {:answer/id #uuid "91706d7f-9e8a-5422-b22f-87c5a31ce844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91706d7f-9e8a-5422-b22f-87c5a31ce844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473249} :answer-field/id #uuid "593b16f1-4d27-5166-8ce1-b30a6106b5da" :answer-field/key "$(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4210865a-e3a8-5e71-9b91-b13bec526e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473250} {:answer/id #uuid "f66dc970-92e8-5c92-af11-07a05ff6fbfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4210865a-e3a8-5e71-9b91-b13bec526e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473250} :answer-field/id #uuid "f52e015f-dbdf-5261-95a7-ded6f4b759d9" :answer-field/key "$(0,\\frac{\\pi }{6})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7a43b0f-4e1d-534a-90fb-daba35eb204c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473252} {:answer/id #uuid "0ee0427c-9b1c-5ebb-9c5f-1221bdc2787f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7a43b0f-4e1d-534a-90fb-daba35eb204c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473252} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b8a6bf9-9b40-5e7a-aaf4-66eefb30e4be" :answer-field/key "$(-\\sqrt{3},\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4f72c98d-40b3-587a-b743-ac6b3ce0ce19" :question/math-academy-id "q-70788" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points.  \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},0)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\sqrt{3},\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{2\\pi }{3},-\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\sqrt{3},\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7eacaa-2cf2-5cae-a40c-737c98124bcf" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Degree of a Homogeneous Polynomial Using the Fast Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec0311ce-b46b-5035-833a-cea67a498994" 