nly if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is not reflexive. For example, $3∣3.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not symmetric. For example, $9∤3$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not transitive. For example, $3∤2$ and $2∤9,$ but $3∣9.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is not an equivalence relation since it's neither reflexive nor symmetric nor transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6302f81d-4834-56a5-b014-0a97c3dccd6f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About General Solutions of Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4049eacb-f333-5928-be15-ad4db6bd4e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474308} {:answer/id #uuid "35601916-369e-51fe-abf4-791c123c637e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35601916-369e-51fe-abf4-791c123c637e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474309} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b95782b-8b17-5f77-9801-8a99d11ccf2a" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8d5ec7-084e-5c9f-8f80-d0e39dff32c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474310} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e17bc7-fee0-5214-bbe1-e420ad24d8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b8d5ec7-084e-5c9f-8f80-d0e39dff32c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474310} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a78c060-c106-55f9-a38d-38117b0a316f" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{4}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45cf437a-d3e6-5bff-a122-cc094f36db9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474312} {:answer/id #uuid "91b92ce5-41cb-5b8f-8a7e-42023c7326d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45cf437a-d3e6-5bff-a122-cc094f36db9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474312} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc403eaf-5b3a-598a-b3ae-28f5e22f4037" :answer-field/key "The general solution of the equation is $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70cf3885-2e2c-5971-b49c-1988c3e0bb2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130004" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}-2y=0,$ where $x>0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\left(\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\right)+2x\\left(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}=0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is a solution to the equation” is true.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =12{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(12{x}^{2})+2x(4{x}^{3})-2{x}^{4}=18{x}^{4}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{4}$ is a solution to the equation” is false.\n\n- So, ${y}_{1}$ is a solution but ${y}_{2}$ is not a solution of the equation, hence $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$ is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement “The general solution of the equation is $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421821 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6302f81d-4834-56a5-b014-0a97c3dccd6f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About General Solutions of Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4025a2da-8220-50a7-b4f3-219e6d29cc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474302} {:answer/id #uuid "91c226a9-4c73-5b94-92b0-1a733df3a834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4025a2da-8220-50a7-b4f3-219e6d29cc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474302} :answer-field/id #uuid "f318ba66-ccb9-5f8e-9231-0f5fb32052aa" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb83e9ac-cb3a-5dc7-8842-0118c6b9c9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474304} {:answer/id #uuid "74a023e8-6ba2-5b3f-a47a-189a8481e140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74a023e8-6ba2-5b3f-a47a-189a8481e140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474305} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf5c45ac-f6f4-5fdf-87b6-c55e5d17a5ea" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab0e9691-308c-596d-9c85-fd9d5dd60a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474306} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2a6d79-cf64-517d-a658-e230018451ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab0e9691-308c-596d-9c85-fd9d5dd60a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474306} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a04d4f0-4217-55ed-ab79-e4478a4fd20e" :answer-field/key "The general solution of the equation is $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fd65812-f6ae-584d-bfe8-d11797aed930" :question/math-academy-id "q-130000" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}-4y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =(1+x){e}^{x} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =(2+x){e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n(2+x){e}^{x}-4(x{e}^{x})=(2-3x){e}^{x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation” is false.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =2{e}^{2x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n4{e}^{2x}-4{e}^{2x}=0.\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation” is true.\n\n- So, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution while ${y}_{2}$ is a solution of the equation, hence $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$ is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement “The general solution of the equation is $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b14560-29f9-58fc-ac65-5505987579fb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Situations That Can Be Modeled as a Discrete Uniform Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14ecc36-432b-56ec-87ab-282eea355b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475002} {:answer/id #uuid "d834568e-ce97-583c-8040-fc4e266d52c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b14ecc36-432b-56ec-87ab-282eea355b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475002} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdad22ae-e385-521b-b788-7347685ca5ee" :answer-field/key "The temperature of a town on a certain day." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475427} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12cca481-ff11-55c7-91de-86d18673b2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475004} {:answer/id #uuid "e8dfccef-97df-539d-8b11-97c54d234ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12cca481-ff11-55c7-91de-86d18673b2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475004} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c49dca-0d5f-5b4f-bddf-bbbd54a75e97" :answer-field/key "The number of letters of a word randomly selected from an English dictionary." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09154e84-c363-5ed7-a1c0-e945e77a7a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475006} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd75d4f-b796-573f-80aa-522e963beda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09154e84-c363-5ed7-a1c0-e945e77a7a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475006} :answer-field/id #uuid "044a1424-5108-5da5-9fee-69fd6070dd31" :answer-field/key "The number of typos in a randomly selected book." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "239e34ce-3c73-5bae-b143-3d41bff8bf51" :question/math-academy-id "q-97754" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We can use the discrete uniform distribution to model the outcome of a single event when the support $S$ is finite, and each $x\\in S$ is equally likely.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The temperature of a town on a certain day” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because a temperature is a real number, so the support is not finite.\n\n- Random variable “The number of letters of a word randomly selected from an English dictionary” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. Each outcome is not equally likely (there are more short words than very long words, for example).\n\n- Random variable “The number of typos in a randomly selected book” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because the number of typos can be any positive integer. Moreover, each outcome is not equally likely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157307 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a25bce44-98ca-54c6-a59f-b7508880d5ba" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Number is Divisible by 4"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dca59057-55b3-5c7c-ba82-222cb932dc6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474314} {:answer/id #uuid "342f9c82-98c2-5afb-b7a9-9344138494ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "342f9c82-98c2-5afb-b7a9-9344138494ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474315} :answer-field/id #uuid "05842590-b751-527d-8067-eab1f70de64f" :answer-field/key "The digit $2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f310f8e-7033-5033-b9d9-74deb0062dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474316} {:answer/id #uuid "24a3dcba-c4be-52f2-90b2-c17076b17071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f310f8e-7033-5033-b9d9-74deb0062dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474316} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1bc1d48-f507-5a60-be9b-0a75bcfd5e98" :answer-field/key "The digit $4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475084} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9415377-7ec5-59cd-9991-c2e930e3248f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474318} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6bb4b7-c675-5ffc-b1be-2557bc730c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9415377-7ec5-59cd-9991-c2e930e3248f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474318} :answer-field/id #uuid "383cae21-cf51-5ade-8876-457d8c7e788a" :answer-field/key "The digit $8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef2c41de-4b26-57f5-bd27-cd0dbe211bfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-131860" :question/problem "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $123\\,321\\,87◻$ divisible by $4?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $4$ if the last two digits form a number that is divisible by $4.$\n\nThe last two digits of the number $123\\,321\\,87◻$ are $7◻.$\n\n- If $2$ is substituted into the blank, then the last two digits are $72,$ which is indeed divisible by $4.$\n\n- If $4$ is substituted into the blank, then the last two digits are $74,$ which is *not* divisible by $4.$\n\n- If $8$ is substituted into the blank, then the last two digits are $78,$ which is *not* divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The digit $2$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa2f2ccb-45b0-5d6a-aa94-ac3eb95c745b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates of More Than One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f548d9d7-5c43-5510-85e7-89f665103530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474544} {:answer/id #uuid "299c3818-e21a-5d63-9d43-edb435384b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "299c3818-e21a-5d63-9d43-edb435384b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474545} :answer-field/id #uuid "33029c5d-a58f-5846-b20f-d30fb9ae1431" :answer-field/key "$P(y):$ ${y}^{2}-1=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cffbbad6-2ff2-508a-a394-ef1effcca096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474546} {:answer/id #uuid "966aa064-e076-50ec-9fdb-88187a6d9994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cffbbad6-2ff2-508a-a394-ef1effcca096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474546} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb33668-d751-5e1f-a8f1-d04525bc5ad1" :answer-field/key "$Q(a,b):$ ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475199} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3099e3c-5a65-5e1b-a4c9-9aceb7935c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474548} {:answer/id #uuid "517d0ea8-bd34-5d06-9d04-f78f5ae6a208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "517d0ea8-bd34-5d06-9d04-f78f5ae6a208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474549} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bc37e72-ebc3-54f5-abd0-30ce43dacb22" :answer-field/key "$R(x,y):$ $\\frac{x}{y}\\in N\\cap Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86866e7c-73c9-5409-8743-b71ad4d3cbe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-175366" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option “$P(y):$ ${y}^{2}-1=8$” is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option “$Q(a,b):$ ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}$” is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(a,b)$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option “$R(x,y):$ $\\frac{x}{y}\\in N\\cap Q$” is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(x,y)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$P(y):$ ${y}^{2}-1=8$”; “$R(x,y):$ $\\frac{x}{y}\\in N\\cap Q$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eef6c94a-e496-5891-a2ca-b9ac53696b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474392} {:answer/id #uuid "741b2c42-773e-5ec4-9974-e7e956acbdca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "741b2c42-773e-5ec4-9974-e7e956acbdca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474393} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e8f1f9b-c7ae-59c4-9600-fc6d84220816" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d17410a8-6d51-5fbd-a6e2-afab502e03a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474394} {:answer/id #uuid "af4458a5-0951-5cde-ba22-486fe27e56df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d17410a8-6d51-5fbd-a6e2-afab502e03a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474394} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d41f5c7-38fe-52a2-ac70-78a54dd7e7be" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45d41db6-c839-5651-be71-5da1d3518353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474396} {:answer/id #uuid "7c8c5f95-5115-5b8c-87c7-c97126e15804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45d41db6-c839-5651-be71-5da1d3518353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474396} :answer-field/id #uuid "569f02b4-e8e3-5e5d-a2af-5774202b1895" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1ce1827c-c98c-5481-b210-2bd31e84c14f" :question/math-academy-id "q-143337" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.14$ | $0.16$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.26$ | $0.34$ | $0.05$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.14$ | $0.16$ | $0.05$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.26$ | $0.34$ | $0.05$ | $0.65$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=1)=f(1,1)=0.26.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.65\\cdot 0.4=0.26.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1) & =0.14=0.35\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(0,2) & =0.16\\ne 0.35\\cdot 0.5={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98e36e60-7f4e-5471-9c79-3de0fa9fb055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474254} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd5cedc-0fa5-539c-83af-8334b94a61b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98e36e60-7f4e-5471-9c79-3de0fa9fb055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474254} :answer-field/id #uuid "45f824b7-26f5-51aa-88da-6f8a9190aea6" :answer-field/key "![Diagram I](images/58/589fb32bea6b8957a7898d7a03991e5bf36e4b9592b39bd6bb5bc2c0ee042c0b.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d05a5c0b-7cf8-5741-abe3-5160cf118536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474256} {:answer/id #uuid "eb08479f-5f31-5a03-a005-616f28978efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d05a5c0b-7cf8-5741-abe3-5160cf118536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474256} :answer-field/id #uuid "60c1be91-8261-58d6-be0c-8554e0b3f515" :answer-field/key "![Diagram II](images/46/462f8e01fa8a0d56f18998a67af72a8512d7e37180641fb1de10a8a069fe2b81.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2c29e1d-be92-5d99-b462-8c335808a7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474258} {:answer/id #uuid "ca799662-448d-5eb3-89be-6549746e0a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2c29e1d-be92-5d99-b462-8c335808a7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474258} :answer-field/id #uuid "435b445b-a1d3-5c7e-bda2-9e456fd12252" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/57/57d69ec94f2cdfb8e20d959240983309aac60814ac0f50fba2f7381f04da2429.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61609b84-fa99-5574-b117-b0c4a018b4cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-110456" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents a set that does not contain the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430806 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67683e7d-bf4f-5fdf-8fe5-df996c30e836" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Vectors Is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6f05695-5d5d-5e1b-bfad-77c51f81a863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474374} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc309ff-eb8f-559c-b906-81545a54e0e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcc309ff-eb8f-559c-b906-81545a54e0e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474375} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d94332b-01c8-5d93-bd36-59655b6dc3cf" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df48fe1-4c0e-5788-ae44-be72c3a42df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474376} {:answer/id #uuid "674b056b-93cf-5bbe-ae7e-6ce2c2c14c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df48fe1-4c0e-5788-ae44-be72c3a42df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474376} :answer-field/id #uuid "05746e78-6328-58c4-96d3-034fda58ec6d" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}⊥̸{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99e78717-3155-5738-b52e-432f0cf2cf83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474378} {:answer/id #uuid "f66fe2c1-0155-5688-b8cc-b89a397d5048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f66fe2c1-0155-5688-b8cc-b89a397d5048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474379} :answer-field/id #uuid "453a25c3-916b-52ae-94c1-1cdb5d5d8d36" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f21c5fc-f92d-5b81-95e0-bb89748670fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-140497" :question/problem "$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors shown above. Given that the inner product in the vector space ${R}^{3}$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{2}⟩ & =5(1)(-1)+(1)(7)+2(1)(-1) \\\\  & =-5+7-2 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}⊥̸{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{2},{v}_{3}⟩ & =5(-1)(2)+(7)(0)+2(-1)(-5) \\\\  & =-10+0+10 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, computing the inner product $⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩ & =5(1)(2)+(1)(0)+2(1)(-5) \\\\  & =10+0-10 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\nAs a result, the set $S$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product”; “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4a33807-0dc5-58b8-9e96-d36c211cd17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474200} {:answer/id #uuid "630190b1-87c4-5c43-bc91-504b4950f58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "630190b1-87c4-5c43-bc91-504b4950f58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474201} :answer-field/id #uuid "4790b87e-09c0-53d0-8040-c5d65661c89f" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2983d130-4a1c-5f7c-92f8-2b8f8ef9258b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474202} {:answer/id #uuid "5a01831f-984b-5618-8beb-6e5a83c9d9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a01831f-984b-5618-8beb-6e5a83c9d9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474203} :answer-field/id #uuid "08ee9bbc-f25e-576b-8ecb-a39f90ca2847" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c407a64-fdc1-57ce-9336-528dd1775a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474204} {:answer/id #uuid "b332a85e-6f82-5133-8e3a-be50909f94ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c407a64-fdc1-57ce-9336-528dd1775a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474204} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c2d9797-b732-51a2-940c-b09caf6ff041" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c3a213f9-9ffe-56d7-a8aa-efb68c3978ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-104735" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=3t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t+1,\\,{p}_{3}(t)={t}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $2$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨3t,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(3t){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1}+(3t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{0}+(3t){|}_{1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(3(-1))\\cdot ((-1)+1)+(3(0))\\cdot (0+1)+(3(1))\\cdot (1+1) \\\\  & =6\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨3t,{t}^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =(3t){|}_{-1}\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1){|}_{-1}+(3t){|}_{0}\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1){|}_{0}+(3t){|}_{1}\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(3(-1))\\cdot ((-1)^{2}-1)+(3(0))\\cdot ({0}^{2}-1)+(3(1))\\cdot ({1}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67683e7d-bf4f-5fdf-8fe5-df996c30e836" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Vectors Is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f67cf98-c041-56b4-b675-cd6608fe0e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475020} {:answer/id #uuid "0fa3734e-111b-53f2-8ebe-871dfb1f88e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f67cf98-c041-56b4-b675-cd6608fe0e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475020} :answer-field/id #uuid "17fd2243-0f57-5f80-9382-57761ade6958" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}⊥̸{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475436} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e85a7d43-b6d8-581b-9e5f-5f063c7c4b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475022} {:answer/id #uuid "b53eb6b7-af91-5d0b-8d68-a78f87a43b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b53eb6b7-af91-5d0b-8d68-a78f87a43b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475023} :answer-field/id #uuid "623fd893-1fe0-5fbf-984e-f62b33160f96" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113ff175-e867-564a-8a13-cc2d64307b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475024} {:answer/id #uuid "72498a25-b060-53eb-8bae-7190cb5973bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72498a25-b060-53eb-8bae-7190cb5973bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475025} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac4eba3-941d-510f-b8db-bb23b5d39486" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1da803c-87de-5156-b3a7-d636001e9616" :question/math-academy-id "q-99637" :question/problem "$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors shown above. Given that the inner product in the vector space ${R}^{3}$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}⊥̸{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{2}⟩ & =2(2)(1)+3(-1)(1)+(1)(-1) \\\\  & =4-3-1 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{2},{v}_{3}⟩ & =2(1)(0)+3(1)(1)+(-1)(3) \\\\  & =0+3-3 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, computing the inner product $⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩ & =2(2)(0)+3(-1)(1)+(1)(3) \\\\  & =0-3+3 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\nAs a result, the set $S$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product”; “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9434ee35-97a1-5285-97bd-642508f58883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474768} {:answer/id #uuid "2e62f471-e501-527c-a2bf-b58c36ed0de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e62f471-e501-527c-a2bf-b58c36ed0de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474769} :answer-field/id #uuid "f52c9065-8b6f-5163-be58-9a1c7fadbe10" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee5d6baf-53f3-5f60-82f6-8b26db329f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474770} {:answer/id #uuid "87258704-04de-53fe-86be-3991a51c9d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87258704-04de-53fe-86be-3991a51c9d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474771} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f5919f8-4a8b-57fc-ba5e-3d0f046a50c8" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475311} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a4f9e18-0783-5aa4-ba7f-a403d553756b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474772} {:answer/id #uuid "b9af53cc-7fb3-530b-a444-9b33c32f55d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9af53cc-7fb3-530b-a444-9b33c32f55d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474773} :answer-field/id #uuid "da939024-b939-5a26-a4f7-b9817e50d965" :answer-field/key "The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation on $(0,\\infty ).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "248767b0-4e8f-59a2-a18a-6d7a3f7d1129" :question/math-academy-id "q-334262" :question/problem "$$\n4{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+6x{y}^{′}-2y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$” is true. First, we find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x).$ Notice that $\\frac{1}{x}={x}^{-1},$ so we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}\\left(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\right)+6x\\left(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) & =0 \\\\ (\\frac{8}{x}-\\frac{6}{x}-\\frac{2}{x}) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$” is true. First, we find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x).$ Notice that $\\sqrt{x}={x}^{\\frac{1}{2}},$ so we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2})+6x(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2})-2\\sqrt{x} & =0 \\\\ (-{x}^{1/2}+3{x}^{1/2}-2{x}^{1/2}) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation on $(0,\\infty ).$” is true. Both ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of the equation. To check if these functions are linearly independent, we compute the Wronskian:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{x}^{-1} & {x}^{1/2} \\\\ -{x}^{-2} & \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={x}^{-1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-{x}^{1/2}\\cdot (-{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3/2}+{x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the  Wronskian is not identically $0$ on $(0,\\infty ),$ the functions are linearly independent. Hence, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation on $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$”; “${y}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$”; “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation on $(0,\\infty ).$”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bacd32ae-566a-595f-ae61-c7390064179f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474762} {:answer/id #uuid "af9b7df9-824a-5976-8ef0-0ed97e33de24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bacd32ae-566a-595f-ae61-c7390064179f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474762} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b52e612-ea71-5a2e-a81c-18901ac0011f" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9146691-1ccc-57f9-88b9-54805a3f76b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474764} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb64cb4-e2ff-50e2-a176-9905722d9d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bb64cb4-e2ff-50e2-a176-9905722d9d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474765} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7f934a8-f5e6-5690-a1d4-2746d5ccf5fa" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475308} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c25a7c82-ba97-5324-83d9-8843be6f251d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474766} {:answer/id #uuid "97e7e003-0f8d-59ae-a1f3-79ac064de7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25a7c82-ba97-5324-83d9-8843be6f251d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474766} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb9f336-1bf0-5e57-b4b7-e8e56b5843aa" :answer-field/key "The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8005871f-5013-58a1-b9ee-7ef831d491ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-334257" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}-12y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}$ is a solution to the equation” is false. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{12}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\left(\\frac{12}{{x}^{5}}\\right)+2x\\left(-\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}\\right)-12\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\right) & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}} & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is not a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation” is true. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(6x)+2x(3{x}^{2})-12({x}^{3}) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation” is false. Since ${y}_{1}(x)$ is not a solution of the given differential equation, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ don't form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e75041c-d0be-5db2-a0db-7c2c2b57b44e" :knowledge-point/title "Defining the Gamma Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef308e06-992f-56cb-a814-cd6e2eabff6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474230} {:answer/id #uuid "2b21cf5a-1e34-520e-9b32-cc50912a07a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b21cf5a-1e34-520e-9b32-cc50912a07a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474231} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecb6fb3d-cd96-5eec-a8eb-ac08a291bda7" :answer-field/key "$3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{3z-1}}{{e}^{{t}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475041} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8347029-3c1b-5125-804b-ccf6172e683c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474232} {:answer/id #uuid "32c4c54c-28fd-5f78-b386-af8e7132a6d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8347029-3c1b-5125-804b-ccf6172e683c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474232} :answer-field/id #uuid "4639a250-d5bb-53ed-ad1e-c39f6e96a9dd" :answer-field/key "$3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-3}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "078bdafd-6fe4-5612-9cda-fdc4bf25bdd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474234} {:answer/id #uuid "a38e3e27-dc42-59fe-ab1d-da94d35d596d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "078bdafd-6fe4-5612-9cda-fdc4bf25bdd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474234} :answer-field/id #uuid "c352f108-be80-5fd3-9710-17251641c6d4" :answer-field/key "$3{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef7933ca-459a-5897-8c5b-5b08b877b68b" :question/math-academy-id "q-107838" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral $3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{3z-1}}{{e}^{{t}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}t$ matches the definition. We use a substitution $s={t}^{3},$ then $3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t=\\text{d}s.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-1}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3(z-1)+2}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3(z-1)}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}(3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{s}^{z-1}{e}^{-s}\\,\\text{d}s=Γ(z).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Integral $3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-3}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t$ does *not* match the definition. The integrand ${t}^{3z-3}{e}^{-{t}^{3}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\n- Integral $3{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{t}^{3z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$ does *not* match the definition. The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $3{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{3z-1}}{{e}^{{t}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}t$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b483f9f7-47a9-5725-b1f1-fe0ea39a7e96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 6"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b3a1c18-402a-5826-bf79-0dba558c64fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474332} {:answer/id #uuid "6c88f31b-1b8f-5242-b277-9bc33fcc1d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c88f31b-1b8f-5242-b277-9bc33fcc1d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474333} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc5edc77-177d-5283-b4ed-f6d29e6130f3" :answer-field/key "$185\\,346$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475092} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3717d0fa-e38b-5a2c-bc8b-96a33d55cf5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474334} {:answer/id #uuid "a0899615-a369-5445-bb33-8c945624b783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0899615-a369-5445-bb33-8c945624b783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474335} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5341e31-a447-5b11-b208-298c154fcdea" :answer-field/key "$2\\,525\\,934$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a85a5c-42ba-5e88-a569-6fb4ddc389eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474336} {:answer/id #uuid "14c3560a-8a2d-5432-9a2c-f7b3ac672b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14c3560a-8a2d-5432-9a2c-f7b3ac672b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474337} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d54dde0-4790-50de-af67-f644fa4e8182" :answer-field/key "$15\\,070\\,962$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "245a9f1f-3fc0-594c-a273-205b94f4bf02" :question/math-academy-id "q-132405" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $185\\,346$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+8+5+3+4+6=27\n$$\n\nSo, $185\\,346$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $2\\,525\\,934$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n2+5+2+5+9+3+4=30\n$$\n\nSo, $2\\,525\\,934$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $15\\,070\\,962$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+5+0+7+0+9+6+2=30\n$$\n\nSo, $15\\,070\\,962$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $185\\,346$; $2\\,525\\,934$; $15\\,070\\,962$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8fa39c-a982-569a-b2e0-833c51259711" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 3 or 9"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1023f7e6-e59f-53cd-8a5f-2e42ef71c00f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474320} {:answer/id #uuid "2dc32817-8382-5025-99f0-ad2c0c830416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dc32817-8382-5025-99f0-ad2c0c830416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474321} :answer-field/id #uuid "854cc33b-b54c-575b-9aca-53389db721ea" :answer-field/key "$935\\,784$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475086} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74d1237a-6542-55a5-bba7-fcb3cee7fbd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474322} {:answer/id #uuid "b7496172-4f29-5fe4-805a-7e950c38af31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74d1237a-6542-55a5-bba7-fcb3cee7fbd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474322} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0fc41dc-297b-5c9e-a513-996195713837" :answer-field/key "$7\\,391\\,123$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475087} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e200043-d762-5434-a59e-aa9354b7703d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474324} {:answer/id #uuid "91ad8e9e-37ad-5097-9f17-8d7924c4732b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91ad8e9e-37ad-5097-9f17-8d7924c4732b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474325} :answer-field/id #uuid "cef549f3-e13e-5104-8ca9-934b1ad8e331" :answer-field/key "$12\\,144\\,801$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9669189-f542-5fc7-9dce-62db6de9555d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132386" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $3?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $935\\,784$ is\n\n$$\n9+3+5+7+8+4=36,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So, $935\\,784$ is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $7\\,391\\,123$ is\n\n$$\n7+3+9+1+1+2+3=26,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $3.$ So, $7\\,391\\,123$ is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $12\\,144\\,801$ is\n\n$$\n1+2+1+4+4+8+0+1=21,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So,  $12\\,144\\,801$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $935\\,784$; $12\\,144\\,801$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8fa39c-a982-569a-b2e0-833c51259711" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 3 or 9"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80cddcd7-7a10-53d3-a249-589070851828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474326} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa771f6-3a38-59bc-8b6d-35530580e18f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80cddcd7-7a10-53d3-a249-589070851828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474326} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb94287d-7984-5ed4-af67-720f38cb3605" :answer-field/key "$34\\,154\\,119$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8859356-e07c-5d6f-9442-820954e24cc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474328} {:answer/id #uuid "c7dbcfbd-d49d-5299-a267-58bd60023c95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8859356-e07c-5d6f-9442-820954e24cc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474328} :answer-field/id #uuid "be5d16f2-6f01-5966-ad54-bda278e555a9" :answer-field/key "$9\\,173\\,589$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475090} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f0d690b-a2af-51f1-908f-dcffce79cd11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474330} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e4a19a-3b1e-52c2-a9b9-12b81d32f9b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f0d690b-a2af-51f1-908f-dcffce79cd11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474330} :answer-field/id #uuid "619d29e9-1652-56eb-a3ec-9f5d3d435236" :answer-field/key "$733\\,123$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2757e05-6aab-58ae-aed8-77516507381e" :question/math-academy-id "q-132392" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $9?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $9$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $34\\,154\\,119$ is\n\n$$\n3+4+1+5+4+1+1+9=28,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $34\\,154\\,119$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $9\\,173\\,589$ is\n\n$$\n9+1+7+3+5+8+9=42,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $9\\,173\\,589$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $733\\,123$ is\n\n$$\n7+3+3+1+2+3=19,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $733\\,123$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6083824-86d5-51f3-b347-2895e58da839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474816} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e8226e-0172-5d33-9eb5-ed8aacac25ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6083824-86d5-51f3-b347-2895e58da839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474816} :answer-field/id #uuid "32a51cde-4bef-52b2-99da-b68e5b7cd2c8" :answer-field/key "$U=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16e1ada7-48ac-55ea-abdc-58511cd98079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474818} {:answer/id #uuid "937b8e9c-3d28-5737-8eed-9c803640fa7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16e1ada7-48ac-55ea-abdc-58511cd98079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474818} :answer-field/id #uuid "13bfc2a0-134b-5d27-9187-31d9b6d86aed" :answer-field/key "$V=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fb905e-e74d-5d79-b882-03aceed66713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474820} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf0a431-8efe-5df5-ab12-1ca33c633645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04fb905e-e74d-5d79-b882-03aceed66713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474820} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad31b141-6411-5cf5-a477-5373690eb045" :answer-field/key "$W=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cc85c8f-2fc1-51b5-90b3-b4c40aaa9ac5" :question/math-academy-id "q-40288" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n$\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}\\},$ \n$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\},$ and \n$\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}\\},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0,\\,{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0,\\,{w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The set $U$ cannot be orthogonal since it contains  $3$ vectors from ${R}^{2}$ (in which we can have an orthogonal set with at most 2 non-zero vectors). Therefore, $U$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=0+10=10\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=12+3-1=14\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"None of the listed\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8939fd4e-9143-5670-88bd-8cc07ba78e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474804} {:answer/id #uuid "1f7bd588-020c-58f2-8002-3d98aa42963e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f7bd588-020c-58f2-8002-3d98aa42963e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474805} :answer-field/id #uuid "46d6e278-71cc-5c6c-84e1-1a44de6ced6f" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475328} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20b1ad14-42e6-5f89-a978-e663de8dbe37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474806} {:answer/id #uuid "1741c864-e1c8-53da-8ac9-3722443203cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1741c864-e1c8-53da-8ac9-3722443203cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474807} :answer-field/id #uuid "529a1270-4283-5e5f-9c2e-556d73625991" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40345fa1-c3d3-53cb-8cf6-d2c039bdf5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474808} {:answer/id #uuid "35fcb43b-2ff4-5503-984d-99e164dc29df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40345fa1-c3d3-53cb-8cf6-d2c039bdf5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474808} :answer-field/id #uuid "46a9bde4-82ff-51bf-855f-089dad897c86" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46f6694f-8103-554b-a6d3-9a98e8c2973d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34711" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+5{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent” is false, while statements “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” and “The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1ed11d6-e65c-5d13-bf39-31eeca3f4a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474774} {:answer/id #uuid "9628809f-61f4-5b0b-be43-73a2d17c5845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1ed11d6-e65c-5d13-bf39-31eeca3f4a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474774} :answer-field/id #uuid "cca6563a-d8d2-55ed-8656-9999204ed40f" :answer-field/key "${D}_{1}(y)={y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f41c909f-4dc5-5044-876a-c9cde7a61ff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474776} {:answer/id #uuid "928a80de-78d5-5056-b57e-bb3af260f38c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "928a80de-78d5-5056-b57e-bb3af260f38c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474777} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f5e59f-c6cc-5d49-a8d0-669dc55d7901" :answer-field/key "${D}_{2}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b00f23b-f729-5d20-a0df-805e10752102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474778} {:answer/id #uuid "14c5ee9a-b2d0-589f-a7c1-2be947c3bd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b00f23b-f729-5d20-a0df-805e10752102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474778} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca101782-ce64-5ba0-9c47-eb42bff93628" :answer-field/key "${D}_{3}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d7d4653-1949-5012-bba8-de86196b5589" :question/math-academy-id "q-337766" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is ${y}^{2},$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=x,{f}_{1}(x)=-2x,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=3.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $y,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${D}_{2}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7300934-7325-58fc-b00f-7f3c820f4904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474780} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd87543-a3d8-5ab5-8243-86e605cdd362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cd87543-a3d8-5ab5-8243-86e605cdd362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474781} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7d01fed-922a-532a-b59b-9c317d62c9b1" :answer-field/key "${D}_{1}(y)=3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c53b9f19-4219-5a80-980b-d117593be475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474782} {:answer/id #uuid "6086ec45-8d73-5327-9bf6-b351964b8ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c53b9f19-4219-5a80-980b-d117593be475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474782} :answer-field/id #uuid "adc3dd8e-00ac-5bf8-8b62-c54d163b4608" :answer-field/key "${D}_{2}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b661da6-09cd-592a-b6a2-18a16a84dd92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474784} {:answer/id #uuid "24905b70-4e0e-576e-9d3b-a54bf6455c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24905b70-4e0e-576e-9d3b-a54bf6455c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474785} :answer-field/id #uuid "08616a93-0dea-5f68-a402-e3a664f40494" :answer-field/key "${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d74a3e3c-e2b0-50fc-9e27-1744209e35b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337767" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=3$ and ${f}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $y,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)={x}^{2},{f}_{2}(x)=0,{f}_{1}(x)=-1,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${D}_{1}(y)=3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}y$; ${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3776bd7-7901-5119-8781-5fa760852de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474248} {:answer/id #uuid "34be4cdd-980d-5cf7-afb5-69444aae9cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3776bd7-7901-5119-8781-5fa760852de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474248} :answer-field/id #uuid "6957b9f5-0c7f-5370-ba38-a21eb5e797aa" :answer-field/key "$v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475050} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3467e4a5-c790-515b-90e9-e9524b6b5643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474250} {:answer/id #uuid "b70cee36-191b-582b-b0d3-c85411adf943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3467e4a5-c790-515b-90e9-e9524b6b5643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474250} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6d9e9f8-9da1-55b6-8112-a9793448ac85" :answer-field/key "$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475051} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95bccbcb-3a47-5abe-9fa0-82e49506d42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474252} {:answer/id #uuid "270c3557-fa11-5a21-934d-4213ed1483bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "270c3557-fa11-5a21-934d-4213ed1483bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474253} :answer-field/id #uuid "0801da56-074b-503c-9458-9eeace399eb8" :answer-field/key "$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "72a34fdf-b3e5-500c-96f3-76e3e66d1191" :question/math-academy-id "q-109572" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A-2I:$\n\n$$\nA-2I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Again, since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $x$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{v}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-2I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $3$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is “$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70b9be53-9395-5371-8ad7-e19949adab26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474398} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6a58fa-bdda-5f09-9d94-437b257bb9a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70b9be53-9395-5371-8ad7-e19949adab26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474398} :answer-field/id #uuid "c83dbd2a-d3c6-528a-8958-f6e5c019702d" :answer-field/key "$max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{11},\\mu )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3824ed15-0a45-5def-b485-9e17437c3843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474400} {:answer/id #uuid "32980db4-466c-5aff-abb2-12ee818d5f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32980db4-466c-5aff-abb2-12ee818d5f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474401} :answer-field/id #uuid "599d78d3-13a7-5faa-b23f-82c826f49593" :answer-field/key "$min({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{10},\\sigma )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475126} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ef7010-3c1d-51c9-886d-e031be64e3c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474402} {:answer/id #uuid "badcd2b2-3071-557b-b92e-a8403da30f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ef7010-3c1d-51c9-886d-e031be64e3c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474402} :answer-field/id #uuid "482caa84-5ca9-5d2c-85ff-33b19e0b8321" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{11}}{{\\mu }^{2}+{\\sigma }^{2}+1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "673ddc27-8133-50ba-9995-aed461126acc" :question/math-academy-id "q-143551" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{11}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ is unknown and $\\sigma $ is known, which of the following are statistics?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression.\n\n- Expression $max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{11},\\mu )$ is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\n- Expression $min({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{10},\\sigma )$ is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{11}$ and the *known* population standard deviation $\\sigma $ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\n- Expression $\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{11}}{{\\mu }^{2}+{\\sigma }^{2}+1}$ is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $min({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{10},\\sigma )$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd3fd748-f238-59b2-badf-54b6e762836c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e777d0d0-dd29-578c-afe8-acb03722065a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474356} {:answer/id #uuid "091df9c9-cbb1-5c16-be7d-f36f5c49791b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "091df9c9-cbb1-5c16-be7d-f36f5c49791b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474357} :answer-field/id #uuid "77690c3c-9b2f-5d87-9563-d49c973c00ff" :answer-field/key "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{X}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=6}^{10}{X}_{i}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59bcc66-5190-5205-ad14-54a9ec55e8cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474358} {:answer/id #uuid "bf27c658-172e-5ec5-b42e-682082363ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d59bcc66-5190-5205-ad14-54a9ec55e8cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474358} :answer-field/id #uuid "53247d84-9f2d-51fa-beee-fa05f3f84dcb" :answer-field/key "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}\\sqrt{{X}_{i}^{2}-{\\sigma }^{2}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c12a3fa8-7b5c-5de8-a3ac-a97aecf79e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474360} {:answer/id #uuid "eb125691-6204-5b53-a91f-e00cf52d68a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c12a3fa8-7b5c-5de8-a3ac-a97aecf79e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474360} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f2eaa29-a361-59a9-9859-74c9e9186b9b" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{10}}{2}+\\mu $" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d216f49f-dbd6-5da5-81b2-ff39a5445339" :question/math-academy-id "q-139833" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{10}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expression ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{X}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=6}^{10}{X}_{i}$ is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{10}$ only.\n\n- Expression ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}\\sqrt{{X}_{i}^{2}-{\\sigma }^{2}}$ is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$\n\n- Expression $\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{10}}{2}+\\mu $ is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{X}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=6}^{10}{X}_{i}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7112c714-4962-5b16-8f8d-765d0369b202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474460} {:answer/id #uuid "7adf6cf4-eabd-52b6-b653-73e0cbfd7368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7adf6cf4-eabd-52b6-b653-73e0cbfd7368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474461} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd78636a-3835-5942-a3fd-7e0ee14f45cb" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6df957d-bb38-5c53-b163-e6870f5cb3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474462} {:answer/id #uuid "91041c6e-f542-5d01-8196-02c9d9d65543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6df957d-bb38-5c53-b163-e6870f5cb3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474462} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa8eed09-27d9-5e21-8524-a1932ae87109" :answer-field/key "$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb30a766-7900-5d50-86d5-89016ad059f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474464} {:answer/id #uuid "02928f92-aad5-5cb3-9006-996e38c094f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02928f92-aad5-5cb3-9006-996e38c094f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474465} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d43ab0-6331-5687-9312-3d01a7f01c93" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a local maximum of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ec0f059-837e-5e3d-9bb4-8d292f2af4e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163781" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈5+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, let's recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=8$” is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-3$ and\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}|=8.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite” is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-3<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}|=8>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is negative-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a local maximum of $f$” is true. Since the matrix $A$ is negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local maximum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=-3$ and $det(A)=8$”; “$a$ is a local maximum of $f$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32262a1a-bff1-5e94-bcd1-5c7a732a6c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474466} {:answer/id #uuid "27511163-3eb0-5da9-82e4-484d6fa22922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27511163-3eb0-5da9-82e4-484d6fa22922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474467} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffb89c92-951f-50df-b288-923f96cabf37" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=2$ and $det(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45d4031d-2906-5c4f-9490-f1fa02c297d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474468} {:answer/id #uuid "f7192339-db35-51bd-a918-939ffb27ef8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45d4031d-2906-5c4f-9490-f1fa02c297d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474468} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca732c93-4b1e-5d49-a724-0ecdb3340ab3" :answer-field/key "$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bb810d3-ff1a-5452-b8a4-17bfa2b2c0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474470} {:answer/id #uuid "a060bed7-c467-5f14-8795-41afe76eb093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bb810d3-ff1a-5452-b8a4-17bfa2b2c0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474470} :answer-field/id #uuid "f14f34e2-c714-5326-9b9d-13f4ad52f6ef" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a saddle point of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "65b2f5b4-89e0-551f-a08f-1b697ac55d76" :question/math-academy-id "q-163786" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈-2+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, we recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=2$ and $det(A)=3$” is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=2$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2)-1(1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite” is false. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=2>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=3>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is positive-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a saddle point of $f$” is false. Since the matrix $A$ is positive-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local minimum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${a}_{11}=2$ and $det(A)=3$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ce264d-034d-56ae-8c45-60644fea8382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474454} {:answer/id #uuid "b69543a5-9507-55c8-9d7b-79018308daff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b69543a5-9507-55c8-9d7b-79018308daff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474455} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8218bbf-3c1e-52b2-9907-9353e67b32bb" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=1$ and $det(A)=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75d60915-0c29-5e83-8567-179f7fad4c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/id